EXAM_DATA.papers["2002"] = {"id":"2002","year":2002,"label":"2002 旧卷","era":"old","sourceUrl":"https://english-exam.lazynote.cn/kaoyan/paper/2002/","timeLimitMin":180,"scoreMode":"raw","parts":[{"id":"section1","kind":"cloze","title":"Section I 完形填空","directions":"Directions: Read the following text. Choose the best word(s) for each numbered blank and mark A, B, C or D on the ANSWER SHEET . (10 points)","points":10,"passage":{"paragraphs":[{"id":"p-section1-1","text":"Comparisons were drawn between the development of television in the 20th century and the diffusion of printing in the 15th and 16th centuries. Yet much had happened   {{1}}   . As was discussed before, it was not   {{2}}   the 19th century that the newspaper became the dominant pre-electronic   {{3}}   , following in the wake of the pamphlet and the book and in the   {{4}}   of the periodical. It was during the same time that the communications revolution   {{5}}   up, beginning with transport, the railway, and leading   {{6}}   through the telegraph, the telephone, radio, and motion pictures   {{7}}   the 20th century world of the motor car and the airplane. Not everyone sees that process in   {{8}}   . It is important to do so."},{"id":"p-section1-2","text":"It is generally recognized,   {{9}}   , that the introduction of the computer in the early 20th century,   {{10}}   by the invention of the integrated circuit during the 1960s, radically changed the process,   {{11}}   its impact on the media was not immediately   {{12}}   . As time went by, computers became smaller and more powerful, and they became \"personal\" too, as well as   {{13}}   , with display becoming sharper and storage   {{14}}   increasing. They were thought of, like people,   {{15}}   generations, with the distance between generations much   {{16}}   ."},{"id":"p-section1-3","text":"It was within the computer age that the term \"information society\" began to be widely used to describe the   {{17}}   within which we now live. The communications revolution has   {{18}}   both work and leisure and how we think and feel both about place and time, but there have been   {{19}}   views about its economic, political, social and cultural implications. \"Benefits\" have been weighed   {{20}}   \"harmful\" outcomes. And generalizations have proved difficult."}]},"questions":[{"n":1,"stem":"","options":[{"key":"A","text":"between"},{"key":"B","text":"before"},{"key":"C","text":"since"},{"key":"D","text":"later"}],"answer":"A","explanation":{"answer":"A","type":"词义辨析","stemZh":"1.","reason":"锚定两个相隔几百年的时间点 前句给出两个端点——20 世纪的电视与 15-16 世纪的印刷（the development of television in the 20th century and the diffusion of printing in the 15th and 16th centuries），而过去完成时 had happened 强调「在对照之前的这段跨度里」许多事已发生。线索指向「两端点之间」的时间范围。","options":{"A":{"mark":"","note":"between 精准对应「20 世纪电视」与「15-16 世纪印刷」两个端点之间这几百年，与过去完成时 had happened 表达「这段区间里发生了很多」完全吻合。"},"B":{"mark":"","note":"before 要求一个可参照的「在……之前」的时间点，前句给的是「两端」而非「单端」，单独使用 before 既切不准也丢失对照含义。"},"C":{"mark":"","note":"since 表「自……以来一直至今」，而原文要谈的是 15 世纪至 20 世纪「两个历史端点之间」的事，并非一直延续到现在的状态。"},"D":{"mark":"","note":"later 意为「在……之后」，但作者要强调的是两个时间端点「之间」的大量发展，而非晚于其中一个端点。"}},"choiceEn":"","clues":[]}},{"n":2,"stem":"","options":[{"key":"A","text":"after"},{"key":"B","text":"by"},{"key":"C","text":"during"},{"key":"D","text":"until"}],"answer":"D","explanation":{"answer":"D","type":"固定搭配","stemZh":"2.","reason":"强调句框架 it was not ... that ... 本句为强调句 it was not __(2)__ the 19th century that the newspaper became the dominant pre-electronic __(3)__，要被强调的是「直到 19 世纪报纸才成为主导前电子媒介」这个时间点，线索本句内即可定，无须跨句。","options":{"A":{"mark":"","note":"after 与 not 连用只能表「不在……之后」，不能构成「直到 19 世纪才……」的强调含义。"},"B":{"mark":"","note":"by 表「到某时为止」，常配完成时；这里强调的是某动作发生的时间节点（became），by 与「直到才」语义不符。"},"C":{"mark":"","note":"during 表「在……期间」，与 not 连用既不构成固定强调句，又无法表达「直到 19 世纪才」的转折时点。"},"D":{"mark":"","note":"until 与 it was not...that 共同构成 it was not until + 时间 + that 句型，意为「直到 19 世纪报纸才成为主导的前电子媒介」，与紧随其后的「following in the wake of the pamphlet and the book」时间线吻合。"}},"choiceEn":"","clues":[]}},{"n":3,"stem":"","options":[{"key":"A","text":"means"},{"key":"B","text":"method"},{"key":"C","text":"medium"},{"key":"D","text":"measure"}],"answer":"C","explanation":{"answer":"C","type":"词义辨析","stemZh":"3.","reason":"「报纸」是传播信息的载体 the newspaper became the dominant pre-electronic __(3)__, following in the wake of the pamphlet and the book：报纸、小册子、书都是传播信息的载体（媒介），且修饰语 pre-electronic（前电子的）正与「电子媒介」对应。","options":{"A":{"mark":"","note":"means 表「手段、方法」，可说 means of communication（交流手段），但 pre-electronic medium 是固定表「前电子时代媒介」的术语，means 不与 pre-electronic 搭配。"},"B":{"mark":"","note":"method 指做事的「方法、步骤」，与报纸作为传播载体的身份对不上，也无 pre-electronic method 的惯用搭配。"},"C":{"mark":"","note":"medium 即「媒介、媒体」，pre-electronic medium 意为「前电子时代的媒介」，与报纸、小册子、书的并列身份完全吻合，且承接全文「communications revolution」的话题术语。"},"D":{"mark":"","note":"measure 表「措施、衡量标准」，与「报纸是何种身份的信息载体」无关。"}},"choiceEn":"","clues":[]}},{"n":4,"stem":"","options":[{"key":"A","text":"process"},{"key":"B","text":"company"},{"key":"C","text":"light"},{"key":"D","text":"form"}],"answer":"B","explanation":{"answer":"B","type":"固定搭配","stemZh":"4.","reason":"与 in the wake of 形成并列 following in the wake of the pamphlet and the book and in the __(4)__ of the periodical：「紧随小册子和书之后，并和期刊__一起__」，这里 and 连接两个介词短语，逻辑上是并列伴随。","options":{"A":{"mark":"","note":"process 与 of 搭配通常是 in the process of doing sth（正在做……的过程中），后接动名词而非名词，与 the periodical 这一具体载体名词搭配不当。"},"B":{"mark":"","note":"company 与 in the ___ of 构成 in the company of「与……为伴／一起」，呼应前半 following in the wake of（紧随其后）的并列伴随逻辑，整体意思是「报纸紧随小册子和书之后，并与期刊为伴」，自然顺畅。"},"C":{"mark":"","note":"light 与 of 搭配成 in the light of「鉴于、根据」，引出依据或缘由，但报纸不是「鉴于期刊」才成为主导媒介，逻辑指向相反。"},"D":{"mark":"","note":"form 与 of 搭配成 in the form of「以……的形式」，但报纸并不「以期刊的形式」存在——它本身就是与期刊不同的另一种载体。"}},"choiceEn":"","clues":[]}},{"n":5,"stem":"","options":[{"key":"A","text":"gathered"},{"key":"B","text":"speeded"},{"key":"C","text":"worked"},{"key":"D","text":"picked"}],"answer":"B","explanation":{"answer":"B","type":"固定搭配","stemZh":"5.","reason":"革命要「加速发展」 It was during the same time that the communications revolution __(5)__ up, beginning with transport, the railway, and leading __(6)__ through the telegraph, the telephone, radio, and motion pictures：随后列举一连串发明，呈现的是节奏越来越快的发展势头，最贴近「提速」一义。","options":{"A":{"mark":"","note":"gathered up 多指收拢物品或勇气，与「通信革命」这一历史进程的主语搭不上。"},"B":{"mark":"","note":"speeded up = 加快、提速，正好对应下文铁路、电报、电话、广播、电影一连串相继出现的「加速发展」势头，是历史叙事中的标准表述。"},"C":{"mark":"","note":"worked up 通常表「激起、激动」，主语多为情绪或人，与「通信革命」这一抽象进程的搭配生硬。"},"D":{"mark":"","note":"picked up 虽有「好转、增速」义，但更偏向「从低谷回升」，且常用于经济或具体活动，与表述「持续加速的通信革命」相比不如 speed up 直接、地道。"}},"choiceEn":"","clues":[]}},{"n":6,"stem":"","options":[{"key":"A","text":"on"},{"key":"B","text":"out"},{"key":"C","text":"over"},{"key":"D","text":"off"}],"answer":"A","explanation":{"answer":"A","type":"固定搭配","stemZh":"6.","reason":"下文 through ... into 描绘连续推进 leading __(6)__ through the telegraph, the telephone, radio, and motion pictures __(7)__ the 20th century world of the motor car and the airplane：through 串起多项发明，最终通向 20 世纪的汽车飞机世界，呈现「不断向前推进」的过程。","options":{"A":{"mark":"","note":"on 与 lead 构成 lead on「继续向前」，且与下文 through ... into 的递进路径完美呼应，整体意为「（革命）从交通铁路开始，一路向前经电报、电话、广播、电影进入 20 世纪汽车飞机时代」。"},"B":{"mark":"","note":"out 与 lead 搭配通常表「领出、引出（某人）」，要求宾语在内，与本句「沿历史推进」的方向不符。"},"C":{"mark":"","note":"over 与 lead 不构成「继续向前推进」的标准短语，且 over 偏「越过、跨过」，与连续贯穿多项发明的语义不符。"},"D":{"mark":"","note":"off 与 lead 构成 lead off「带头、开始」，但句中「beginning with transport」已明示起点，此处需要的是「继续向前」而非再次「开始」。"}},"choiceEn":"","clues":[]}},{"n":7,"stem":"","options":[{"key":"A","text":"of"},{"key":"B","text":"for"},{"key":"C","text":"beyond"},{"key":"D","text":"into"}],"answer":"D","explanation":{"answer":"D","type":"固定搭配","stemZh":"7.","reason":"lead on through ... 终点在「20 世纪世界」 本句承上 leading __(6)__ through the telegraph, the telephone, radio, and motion pictures __(7)__ the 20th century world of the motor car and the airplane：lead on through ... 串起一系列发明，最终的「落脚点」就是「20 世纪汽车飞机世界」这个新阶段。","options":{"A":{"mark":"","note":"of 表「……的」，会让句子变成「电影属于 20 世纪世界」的修饰关系，丢掉了「贯穿历史进入新时代」的动态推进感。"},"B":{"mark":"","note":"for 表「为了、对……来说」，无法承接「lead on through」的推进路径，逻辑断裂。"},"C":{"mark":"","note":"beyond 表「超出、越过」，会变成「越过 20 世纪世界」，而下文紧接的就是 20 世纪的进程（电脑等），方向相反。"},"D":{"mark":"","note":"into 表「进入」，与前文 lead on through 串起的推进路径完美收束：贯穿电报、电话、广播、电影，进入 20 世纪汽车飞机的世界，最自然、最地道。"}},"choiceEn":"","clues":[]}},{"n":8,"stem":"","options":[{"key":"A","text":"concept"},{"key":"B","text":"dimension"},{"key":"C","text":"effect"},{"key":"D","text":"perspective"}],"answer":"D","explanation":{"answer":"D","type":"词义辨析","stemZh":"8.","reason":"本段宏大的「过程」需被通盘审视 前文 beginning with transport, the railway, and leading __(6)__ through the telegraph, the telephone, radio, and motion pictures __(7)__ the 20th century world of the motor car and the airplane 描绘了一个跨数百年的宏大进程，作者随即评论 Not everyone sees that process in __(8)__. It is important to do so. 表示要从整体视角看待这一进程。","options":{"A":{"mark":"","note":"concept 意为「概念」，see ... in concept 不是惯用搭配，且语义指向是「以概念形式看」，与「从整体视角审视进程」不符。"},"B":{"mark":"","note":"dimension 表「维度、方面」，see sth in dimension 不是固定搭配，也无法表达「整体审视」的意思。"},"C":{"mark":"","note":"effect 与 in 搭配是 in effect「实际上、生效」，意思与「看待过程的视角」对不上，逻辑跳脱。"},"D":{"mark":"","note":"perspective 与 in 构成 see ... in perspective「以恰当/整体的视角看」，与下文 It is important to do so. 强调「应当这么看」遥相呼应，是地道写法。"}},"choiceEn":"","clues":[]}},{"n":9,"stem":"","options":[{"key":"A","text":"indeed"},{"key":"B","text":"hence"},{"key":"C","text":"however"},{"key":"D","text":"therefore"}],"answer":"C","explanation":{"answer":"C","type":"逻辑关系","stemZh":"9.","reason":"由「并非人人都从整体视角看」转入「但人们普遍承认……」 上段末 Not everyone sees that process in __(8)__. It is important to do so. 暗含「很多人没意识到这一点」；本段开头 It is generally recognized, __(9)__, that the introduction of the computer...radically changed the process 却说「人们普遍承认计算机的引入彻底改变了进程」，前后构成转折。","options":{"A":{"mark":"","note":"indeed 表「确实、的确」，是对上文的进一步肯定，但此处上下文是对比（并非人人能看清 vs 但人们普遍承认计算机带来的改变），不是同向加强。"},"B":{"mark":"","note":"hence 表「因此、由此」，需要明确因果链，但「并非人人整体看待」并不导致「人们普遍承认计算机改变了进程」，逻辑断。"},"C":{"mark":"","note":"however 表「然而」，对上段的「并非人人都能整体看待」给出转折——「然而，计算机的影响是普遍被承认的」，符合作者在分项肯定中保留批评的语气。"},"D":{"mark":"","note":"therefore 表「因此」，要求前因后果，但上下文不是因果，而是对比关系。"}},"choiceEn":"","clues":[]}},{"n":10,"stem":"","options":[{"key":"A","text":"brought"},{"key":"B","text":"followed"},{"key":"C","text":"stimulated"},{"key":"D","text":"characterized"}],"answer":"B","explanation":{"answer":"B","type":"词义辨析","stemZh":"10.","reason":"计算机引入「在 20 世纪初」，集成电路发明「在 1960 年代」 本句给了两个时间锚点：the introduction of the computer in the early 20th century 在前，the invention of the integrated circuit during the 1960s 在后，是「先有计算机引入，后被集成电路发明所跟随」的时序关系。","options":{"A":{"mark":"","note":"brought 多与 about/in/on 搭配（bring about=带来），单独 brought by sth 一般指「被某人带来」，且因果方向错（不是集成电路把计算机引入带来的）。"},"B":{"mark":"","note":"followed 与 by 构成「X followed by Y」=X 之后是 Y。计算机引入在 20 世纪初，集成电路在 1960 年代，恰是「先 X 后 Y」的接力关系，结构和时序完美吻合。"},"C":{"mark":"","note":"stimulated by Y 意思是「被 Y 所刺激/推动」，则要求 Y 在 X 之前并推动 X，但事实是 Y（集成电路）晚于 X（计算机引入），方向反。"},"D":{"mark":"","note":"characterized by Y 表「以 Y 为特征」，但 Y 是后来的发明，不能成为 X（计算机引入）的特征，时间逻辑错。"}},"choiceEn":"","clues":[]}},{"n":11,"stem":"","options":[{"key":"A","text":"unless"},{"key":"B","text":"since"},{"key":"C","text":"lest"},{"key":"D","text":"although"}],"answer":"D","explanation":{"answer":"D","type":"逻辑关系","stemZh":"11.","reason":"「彻底改变」VS「冲击并非立即显现」 主句 radically changed the process 是肯定影响，从句 its impact on the media was not immediately __(12)__ 表达「冲击并未立即显现」——一个强一个弱，构成让步对比关系。","options":{"A":{"mark":"","note":"unless 表「除非」，引导否定条件，与「事实陈述+让步」不符，且整段并非在谈条件。"},"B":{"mark":"","note":"since 表「因为」，会被理解为「因为冲击并未立即显现，所以彻底改变了进程」，因果关系荒谬。"},"C":{"mark":"","note":"lest 表「以免、唯恐」，后接虚拟语气，整句变成「彻底改变进程以免冲击不显」，语义荒谬。"},"D":{"mark":"","note":"although 表「虽然」，引导让步：「计算机的引入彻底改变了进程，虽然其对媒体的影响并未立刻显现」，恰好处理「强主句+弱从句」的让步反差。"}},"choiceEn":"","clues":[]}},{"n":12,"stem":"","options":[{"key":"A","text":"apparent"},{"key":"B","text":"desirable"},{"key":"C","text":"negative"},{"key":"D","text":"plausible"}],"answer":"A","explanation":{"answer":"A","type":"词义辨析","stemZh":"12.","reason":"下文随时间逐步显化 紧随其后：As time went by, computers became smaller and more powerful, and they became \"personal\" too：随着时间推移，计算机才慢慢变小变强、变得个人化——意味着「冲击不是立即明显的，而是慢慢明显起来」。","options":{"A":{"mark":"","note":"apparent 表「明显的」，not immediately apparent = 不是立即明显的，恰好对应下文 As time went by, computers became smaller and more powerful 「随时间逐步显化」的过程。"},"B":{"mark":"","note":"desirable 表「值得拥有的、可取的」，含价值评价；本句客观陈述影响出现的快慢，没有「是否值得」的态度。"},"C":{"mark":"","note":"negative 表「负面的」，但作者在此并未把计算机影响定性为负面，下文也未提供负面证据，色彩不符。"},"D":{"mark":"","note":"plausible 表「似乎合理的」，多用于判断说法是否站得住脚，而非描述「影响是否显现」，搭配不切。"}},"choiceEn":"","clues":[]}},{"n":13,"stem":"","options":[{"key":"A","text":"institutional"},{"key":"B","text":"universal"},{"key":"C","text":"fundamental"},{"key":"D","text":"instrumental"}],"answer":"A","explanation":{"answer":"A","type":"词义辨析","stemZh":"13.","reason":"与「个人化」形成场景对照 they became \"personal\" too, as well as __(13)__：personal 用了引号特意点明「个人使用」，而 as well as 引出与之并列的另一种使用主体，逻辑指向「另一类使用场景」。","options":{"A":{"mark":"","note":"institutional 表「机构的」，与 personal「个人的」构成「使用主体」轴上的并列对照——计算机既个人化，也机构化，与历史事实和上下文都吻合。"},"B":{"mark":"","note":"universal 表「普遍的、通用的」，描述的是「普及程度」而非「使用主体」，与 personal 不是同一对照轴。"},"C":{"mark":"","note":"fundamental 表「基础的、根本的」，描述重要性，与 personal 这一「使用场景」标签不在同一维度，无法并列。"},"D":{"mark":"","note":"instrumental 表「起作用的、有助益的」，强调功能贡献，与 personal 的对照面对不上。"}},"choiceEn":"","clues":[]}},{"n":14,"stem":"","options":[{"key":"A","text":"ability"},{"key":"B","text":"capability"},{"key":"C","text":"capacity"},{"key":"D","text":"faculty"}],"answer":"C","explanation":{"answer":"C","type":"词义辨析","stemZh":"14.","reason":"storage 谈的是「能装多少」 display becoming sharper and storage __(14)__ increasing：display sharper 谈显示「更清晰」，storage 自然谈「容量越来越大」，与硬盘/内存的容量增长事实一致。","options":{"A":{"mark":"","note":"ability 强调主语「会做某事」的能力，多接 to do sth，与 storage 这种「容器属性」搭配不准。"},"B":{"mark":"","note":"capability 表「（潜在的）能力、性能」，强调系统能做什么，与「存储多少」这个量化容量义有别。"},"C":{"mark":"","note":"capacity 表「容量、容积」，storage capacity「存储容量」是 IT 领域常用术语；与下文 increasing「不断增大」一拍即合：存储容量持续增长。"},"D":{"mark":"","note":"faculty 多指人的「（智力、感知）官能」或大学「院系」，与计算机存储毫无关联。"}},"choiceEn":"","clues":[]}},{"n":15,"stem":"","options":[{"key":"A","text":"by means of"},{"key":"B","text":"in terms of"},{"key":"C","text":"with regard to"},{"key":"D","text":"in line with"}],"answer":"B","explanation":{"answer":"B","type":"固定搭配","stemZh":"15.","reason":"「像人一样按代际理解」 They were thought of, like people, __(15)__ generations, with the distance between generations much __(16)__：作者把计算机比作人，按「代际」这一概念来理解，本句内即可定，无须跨句。","options":{"A":{"mark":"","note":"by means of 意为「凭借、通过」，引出工具/手段，但 generations「代际」不是手段而是「理解维度」，搭配不切。"},"B":{"mark":"","note":"in terms of 表「按……来看、从……角度」，think of ... in terms of generations 即「按代际理解」，与「像人一样按代际划分」完全吻合。"},"C":{"mark":"","note":"with regard to 意为「关于、就……而言」，引出话题对象，而非「划分维度」，与本句「按代际划分」的角度框架义不符。"},"D":{"mark":"","note":"in line with 意为「与……一致、符合」，要求后接「标准/原则」，但 generations 不是标准，与「按代际理解」语义不切。"}},"choiceEn":"","clues":[]}},{"n":16,"stem":"","options":[{"key":"A","text":"deeper"},{"key":"B","text":"fewer"},{"key":"C","text":"nearer"},{"key":"D","text":"smaller"}],"answer":"D","explanation":{"answer":"D","type":"词义辨析","stemZh":"16.","reason":"代际间隔越来越短 上一空 __(15)__ generations 已经把计算机的更新换代比作「代际」，本句 with the distance between generations much __(16)__ 自然描绘代际之间的「间隔」，而计算机更新越来越快，间隔自然越来越短/小。","options":{"A":{"mark":"","note":"deeper 表「更深」，描述纵深，但 distance 谈的是「间隔大小」，二者不是同一维度。"},"B":{"mark":"","note":"fewer 只能修饰可数名词（fewer generations 才行），不能修饰 distance（不可数概念），语法错。"},"C":{"mark":"","note":"nearer 表「更近」，多形容物体「靠得更近」，主语应是物体本身，而非 distance；distance nearer 搭配不地道。"},"D":{"mark":"","note":"smaller 表「更小」，distance much smaller「间隔小得多」是表示「代际间隔越来越短」的地道写法，与计算机更新越来越快的事实趋势一致。"}},"choiceEn":"","clues":[]}},{"n":17,"stem":"","options":[{"key":"A","text":"context"},{"key":"B","text":"range"},{"key":"C","text":"scope"},{"key":"D","text":"territory"}],"answer":"A","explanation":{"answer":"A","type":"词义辨析","stemZh":"17.","reason":"「我们生活其中的」=语境/环境 the __(17)__ within which we now live：定语从句明示「我们生活在其中」，说明这是一个能容纳我们生活的「整体语境/环境」，与 information society 这一时代概念一致。","options":{"A":{"mark":"","note":"context 表「（社会/时代）背景、语境」，描述我们生活的整体时代环境，与「信息社会」概念和 within which we now live 完全契合。"},"B":{"mark":"","note":"range 表「范围、幅度」，多用于具体量值的跨度（temperature range、price range），不指人所「生活其中」的时代背景。"},"C":{"mark":"","note":"scope 多指研究、活动的「范围、视野」，与「我们身处其中的时代环境」的整体感不同。"},"D":{"mark":"","note":"territory 多指地理领土或学科领域，不指抽象的「时代背景/语境」。"}},"choiceEn":"","clues":[]}},{"n":18,"stem":"","options":[{"key":"A","text":"regarded"},{"key":"B","text":"impressed"},{"key":"C","text":"influenced"},{"key":"D","text":"effected"}],"answer":"C","explanation":{"answer":"C","type":"词义辨析","stemZh":"18.","reason":"革命对生活方方面面起作用 The communications revolution has __(18)__ both work and leisure and how we think and feel both about place and time：宾语横跨工作、休闲、时空感受，明显是「广泛影响」的语义场。","options":{"A":{"mark":"","note":"regarded 表「看作、认为」，多接 sb as sth，主语用「革命」去「看作」工作和闲暇不合理。"},"B":{"mark":"","note":"impressed 表「使……印象深刻」，宾语通常是人；impress work and leisure 不符合英语惯用。"},"C":{"mark":"","note":"influenced 表「影响」，与广宾语「工作、闲暇、对地点时间的思考与感受」完全匹配，是描述通信革命影响生活方方面面的最自然选择。"},"D":{"mark":"","note":"effected 作动词表「实现、使发生」，宾语通常是 change/reform，而非 work and leisure；此处易与 affect 形近混淆，但词义不同。"}},"choiceEn":"","clues":[]}},{"n":19,"stem":"","options":[{"key":"A","text":"competitive"},{"key":"B","text":"controversial"},{"key":"C","text":"distracting"},{"key":"D","text":"irrational"}],"answer":"B","explanation":{"answer":"B","type":"词义辨析","stemZh":"19.","reason":"权益对照「Benefits vs harmful outcomes」 本句紧随其后：\"Benefits\" have been weighed __(20)__ \"harmful\" outcomes. And generalizations have proved difficult. 「益处」与「害处」被放在天平两端，且作者点明「难以一概而论」——明确指向「观点分歧、有争议」。","options":{"A":{"mark":"","note":"competitive 多指市场/比赛竞争性，与「观点彼此对立」是近邻但不准——观点之间是分歧争议而非「竞争」。"},"B":{"mark":"","note":"controversial 表「有争议的、引起对立看法的」，与下文 Benefits vs harmful、generalizations have proved difficult 完美呼应，是描述「对其经济、政治、社会、文化影响存在不同看法」的最佳词。"},"C":{"mark":"","note":"distracting 表「使分心」，描述对象通常是噪音/事件，不能修饰「观点」。"},"D":{"mark":"","note":"irrational 表「非理性的」，色彩过重，且作者并未否定这些观点的理性基础，只是说存在分歧。"}},"choiceEn":"","clues":[]}},{"n":20,"stem":"","options":[{"key":"A","text":"above"},{"key":"B","text":"upon"},{"key":"C","text":"against"},{"key":"D","text":"with"}],"answer":"C","explanation":{"answer":"C","type":"固定搭配","stemZh":"20.","reason":"「益处」与「害处」对立权衡 \"Benefits\" have been weighed __(20)__ \"harmful\" outcomes：benefits 与 harmful outcomes 是相反两极，自然构成「权衡比较」关系；本句内即可定，无需跨句。","options":{"A":{"mark":"","note":"above 表「在……之上」，与 weigh 搭配会变成「比 harmful outcomes 更重要」，但作者并未给出谁更重的定论，且这不是 weigh 的标准搭配。"},"B":{"mark":"","note":"upon 与 weigh 构成 weigh upon「使（人）忧虑/有压力」，主语应是负担，宾语是人，与「利弊权衡」语义完全错位。"},"C":{"mark":"","note":"against 与 weigh 构成 weigh A against B「把 A 与 B 对比权衡」，正好处理 benefits 与 harmful outcomes 这一组利弊对照，意思自然、搭配地道。"},"D":{"mark":"","note":"with 与 weigh 没有「权衡利弊」的固定搭配，且 weigh with sb 多义为「对……有分量、被……重视」，与本句宾语 harmful outcomes 搭不上。"}},"choiceEn":"","clues":[]}}]},{"id":"section2-part-a-1","kind":"reading","title":"Text 1","textNo":1,"directions":"Directions: Read the following four texts. Answer the questions after each text by choosing A, B, C or D. Mark your answers on the ANSWER SHEET . (40 points)","points":10,"passage":{"title":"Text 1","paragraphs":[{"id":"p-section2-part-a-1-1","text":"If you intend using humor in your talk to make people smile, you must know how to identify shared experiences and problems. Your humor must be relevant to the audience and should help to show them that you are one of them or that you understand their situation and are in sympathy with their point of view. Depending on whom you are addressing, the problems will be different. If you are talking to a group of managers, you may refer to the disorganized methods of their secretaries; alternatively if you are addressing secretaries, you may want to comment on their disorganized bosses."},{"id":"p-section2-part-a-1-2","text":"Here is an example, which I heard at a nurses' convention, of a story which works well because the audience all shared the same view of doctors. A man arrives in heaven and is being shown around by St. Peter. He sees wonderful accommodations, beautiful gardens, sunny weather, and so on. Everyone is very peaceful, polite and friendly until, waiting in a line for lunch, the new arrival is suddenly pushed aside by a man in a white coat, who rushes to the head of the line, grabs his food and stomps over to a table by himself. \"Who is that?\" the new arrival asked St. Peter. \"Oh, that's God,\" came the reply, \"but sometimes he thinks he's a doctor.\""},{"id":"p-section2-part-a-1-3","text":"If you are part of the group which you are addressing, you will be in a position to know the experiences and problems which are common to all of you and it'll be appropriate for you to make a passing remark about the inedible canteen food or the chairman's notorious bad taste in ties. With other audiences you mustn't attempt to cut in with humor as they will resent an outsider making disparaging remarks about their canteen or their chairman. You will be on safer ground if you stick to scapegoats like the Post Office or the telephone system."},{"id":"p-section2-part-a-1-4","text":"If you feel awkward being humorous, you must practice so that it becomes more natural. Include a few casual and apparently off-the-cuff remarks which you can deliver in a relaxed and unforced manner. Often it's the delivery which causes the audience to smile, so speak slowly and remember that a raised eyebrow or an unbelieving look may help to show that you are making a light-hearted remark."},{"id":"p-section2-part-a-1-5","text":"Look for the humor. It often comes from the unexpected. A twist on a familiar quote \"If at first you don't succeed, give up\" or a play on words or on a situation. Search for exaggeration and understatement. Look at your talk and pick out a few words or sentences which you can turn about and inject with humor."}]},"questions":[{"n":21,"stem":"To make your humor work, you should____.","options":[{"key":"A","text":"take advantage of different kinds of audience"},{"key":"B","text":"make fun of the disorganized people"},{"key":"C","text":"address different problems to different people"},{"key":"D","text":"show sympathy for your listeners"}],"answer":"C","explanation":{"answer":"C","type":"细节题","stemZh":"为了让你的幽默发挥作用，你应该____。","choicesZh":{"A":"利用不同类型的听众","B":"取笑那些缺乏条理的人","C":"针对不同的人谈论不同的问题","D":"对你的听众表示同情"},"analysis":{"type":"题干 To make your humor work, you should 直接询问让幽默奏效的做法，没有 infer/imply 等推断标志，要找的是文中明示的条件，因此判为细节题。","parse":"To make your humor work, you should____ 是一个由不定式作目的状语领起的不完整陈述句，主句 you should ____ 等待用某个动词短语补全；阅读时把 to make your humor work（要让你的幽默奏效）当作触发条件，把空格当作要找的『做法』即可，结构清晰无陷阱。","locateEn":"Your humor must be relevant to the audience and should help to show them that you are one of them or that you understand their situation and are in sympathy with their point of view. Depending on whom you are addressing, the problems will be different.","locateZh":"你的幽默必须与听众相关，要让他们觉得你是他们中的一员，或你理解他们的处境、与他们的观点产生共鸣；针对不同的对象，谈的问题也应不同。","options":{"A":{"flag":"","note":"take advantage of different kinds of audience 中的 take advantage of（利用/占便宜）在原文中无对应，原文只说要 in sympathy with（共情）听众，不是利用听众。","pairs":[]},"B":{"flag":"","note":"you may refer to the disorganized methods of their secretaries 只是面向经理时的『一种举例』，make fun of the disorganized people 把这个局部例子升级成总建议，与原文范围不符。","pairs":[]},"C":{"flag":"","note":"四个选项里只有 address different problems to different people 同时包含『不同问题』与『不同人』的对应关系，与预判完全吻合，锁定 C。","pairs":[{"orig":"Depending on whom you are addressing, the problems will be different.","opt":"address different problems to different people"}]},"D":{"flag":"","note":"show sympathy for your listeners 与原文 in sympathy with their point of view 有词面关联，但只覆盖『共情』这一手段，遗漏了真正的总条件『针对不同对象谈不同问题』，是部分正确整体错。","pairs":[]}}}}},{"n":22,"stem":"The joke about doctors implies that, in the eyes of nurses, they are____.","options":[{"key":"A","text":"impolite to new arrivals"},{"key":"B","text":"very conscious of their godlike role"},{"key":"C","text":"entitled to some privileges"},{"key":"D","text":"very busy even during lunch hours"}],"answer":"B","explanation":{"answer":"B","type":"推断题","stemZh":"关于医生的笑话暗示，在护士眼中，医生____。","choicesZh":{"A":"对新来的人不礼貌","B":"非常清楚自己如神一般的角色","C":"有权享有某些特权","D":"即使在午餐时间也非常忙碌"},"analysis":{"type":"题干 The joke about doctors implies that 中的 implies 明确告诉考生答案不在字面，要从笑话的情节往上推一步『护士借这个笑话表达对医生的什么看法』。","parse":"The joke about doctors implies that, in the eyes of nurses, they are____ 是 imply that 引导宾语从句的不完整陈述。从句主语 they 回指主句的 doctors，in the eyes of nurses 是插入语，提示判断视角；要补的是表语，描述『护士眼中的医生是怎样的』。","locateEn":"\"Who is that?\" the new arrival asked St. Peter. \"Oh, that's God,\" came the reply, \"but sometimes he thinks he's a doctor.\"","locateZh":"新到的人问圣彼得：『那是谁？』回答说：『噢，那是上帝，但他有时以为自己是医生。』","options":{"A":{"flag":"","note":"impolite to new arrivals 只描述笑话中『把新到者推到一边』这个表面动作，没有触及反讽层；护士借笑话表达的不是『医生对新人无礼』，而是医生的自我神化。","pairs":[]},"B":{"flag":"","note":"选项 very conscious of their godlike role 是唯一一个抓住『医生自比上帝/神』反讽的选项，与预判完全一致，锁定 B。","pairs":[{"orig":"but sometimes he thinks he's a doctor.","opt":"very conscious of their godlike role"}]},"C":{"flag":"","note":"entitled to some privileges 把笑话中的傲慢插队美化为『有权享受某些特权』，与笑话的讽刺基调完全相反——笑话是在嘲讽这种做派，不是承认它的正当性。","pairs":[]},"D":{"flag":"","note":"very busy even during lunch hours 用『午餐时间也忙』来解释插队，但原文没有任何一句暗示医生忙——故事强调的是他的傲慢神态，不是工作强度。","pairs":[]}}}}},{"n":23,"stem":"It can be inferred from the text that public services____.","options":[{"key":"A","text":"have benefited many people"},{"key":"B","text":"are the focus of public attention"},{"key":"C","text":"are an inappropriate subject for humor"},{"key":"D","text":"have often been the laughing stock"}],"answer":"D","explanation":{"answer":"D","type":"推断题","stemZh":"从文中可以推断出，公共服务____。","choicesZh":{"A":"使许多人受益","B":"是公众关注的焦点","C":"是不适合用于幽默的话题","D":"经常成为笑柄"},"analysis":{"type":"It can be inferred from the text that public services 中的 inferred 明确这是推断题：答案需要由原文对公共服务的态度/做法再走一步得出，不会是原文照搬。","parse":"It can be inferred from the text that public services____ 是 It is + 过去分词 + that 从句的形式主语句型，真正主语是 that 从句。从句缺谓语部分，要补的是『公共服务怎么样』，结构平铺直叙无陷阱。","locateEn":"You will be on safer ground if you stick to scapegoats like the Post Office or the telephone system.","locateZh":"如果你坚持把矛头对准邮局或电话系统这类『替罪羊』，你会更稳妥（更安全）。","options":{"A":{"flag":"","note":"have benefited many people 谈的是公共服务的社会贡献，与原文谈论『可调侃对象』的话题完全无关，是答非所问。","pairs":[]},"B":{"flag":"","note":"are the focus of public attention 说公共服务是公众关注的焦点，原文未谈关注度，只谈它是可被调侃的对象，无任何依据。","pairs":[]},"C":{"flag":"","note":"are an inappropriate subject for humor 说公共服务不适合作幽默素材，但原文明确说『把矛头对准它们更稳妥』——它正是合适的素材，方向与原文相反。","pairs":[]},"D":{"flag":"","note":"四个选项中只有 have often been the laughing stock 抓住了 scapegoats 的比喻含义并外推一步『常被嘲笑』，与预判契合。","pairs":[{"orig":"You will be on safer ground if you stick to scapegoats like the Post Office or the telephone system.","opt":"have often been the laughing stock"}]}}}}},{"n":24,"stem":"To achieve the desired result, humorous stories should be delivered____.","options":[{"key":"A","text":"in well-worded language"},{"key":"B","text":"as awkwardly as possible"},{"key":"C","text":"in exaggerated statements"},{"key":"D","text":"as casually as possible"}],"answer":"D","explanation":{"answer":"D","type":"细节题","stemZh":"为了达到预期效果,幽默故事应该____地讲述。","choicesZh":{"A":"用措辞讲究的语言","B":"尽可能笨拙","C":"用夸张的陈述","D":"尽可能随意"},"analysis":{"type":"should be delivered____ 询问应以怎样的方式讲述幽默故事，是作者明示的方法建议，无 imply/infer 词，按细节题处理。","parse":"To achieve the desired result, humorous stories should be delivered____ 是被动语态的不完整陈述：主语 humorous stories 接 should be delivered，空格处补方式状语（多以介词短语或 as ... as possible 形式出现）；To achieve the desired result 是目的状语，告诉考生『要达到预期效果』是判断方式的标准。","locateEn":"Include a few casual and apparently off-the-cuff remarks which you can deliver in a relaxed and unforced manner. Often it's the delivery which causes the audience to smile, so speak slowly and remember that a raised eyebrow or an unbelieving look may help to show that you are making a light-hearted remark.","locateZh":"插入几句随意、看似临场发挥的话，用一种轻松、不刻意的方式讲出来。让听众发笑的往往是讲述方式本身——慢慢说，并且记得：抬一下眉毛或露出难以置信的神情，有助于显示你是在说一句轻松话。","options":{"A":{"flag":"","note":"in well-worded language 强调字斟句酌、措辞讲究，与原文 apparently off-the-cuff remarks（看似临场发挥）方向相反——临场发挥反对的就是字斟句酌。","pairs":[]},"B":{"flag":"","note":"as awkwardly as possible 利用原文首句 If you feel awkward being humorous, you must practice 中 awkward 一词制造干扰；但原文 awkward 是要 practice 去消除的负面状态，不是要追求的讲法。","pairs":[]},"C":{"flag":"","note":"in exaggerated statements 来自第五段 Search for exaggeration and understatement.，是『素材挖掘』的建议，与 delivered 询问的『讲述方式』不在同一话题轴上，属于答非所问。","pairs":[]},"D":{"flag":"","note":"四个选项里只有 as casually as possible 与原文同义群正向对接，强度也合理，锁定 D。","pairs":[{"orig":"Include a few casual and apparently off-the-cuff remarks which you can deliver in a relaxed and unforced manner.","opt":"as casually as possible"}]}}}}},{"n":25,"stem":"The best title for the text may be____.","options":[{"key":"A","text":"Use Humor Effectively"},{"key":"B","text":"Various Kinds of Humor"},{"key":"C","text":"Add Humor to Speech"},{"key":"D","text":"Different Humor Strategies"}],"answer":"A","explanation":{"answer":"A","type":"主旨题","stemZh":"本文最佳标题可能是____。","choicesZh":{"A":"有效运用幽默","B":"各种类型的幽默","C":"为演讲增添幽默","D":"不同的幽默策略"},"analysis":{"type":"The best title for the text may be____ 要求选最佳标题，是典型主旨题；正确项必须覆盖全文，而不是某一段的局部话题。","parse":"The best title for the text may be____ 是简单系表结构，主语 The best title for the text，系动词 may be 后接表语；空格填一个名词性短语作标题，情态动词 may 只是缓和语气、不影响判断。","locateEn":"","locateZh":"","options":{"A":{"flag":"","note":"Use Humor Effectively 是唯一同时覆盖『对象/视角/讲法/素材』全部维度并扣住『让幽默奏效』主线的选项。","pairs":[{"orig":"If you intend using humor in your talk to make people smile, you must know how to identify shared experiences and problems.","opt":"Use Humor Effectively"},{"orig":"Often it's the delivery which causes the audience to smile, so speak slowly","opt":"Use Humor Effectively"}]},"B":{"flag":"","note":"Various Kinds of Humor 暗示本文按『幽默的种类』展开，但全文未做任何分类讨论，只谈如何让幽默奏效。","pairs":[]},"C":{"flag":"","note":"Add Humor to Speech 只覆盖『加入幽默』这一动作的总命题，没有回答全文的核心——『怎么加才奏效』；它是文章的话题层，不是主旨层。","pairs":[]},"D":{"flag":"","note":"Different Humor Strategies 暗示原文罗列『几种不同的幽默策略』并加以比较，但全文呈现的是同一主题下的多面建议，不是策略对比，故覆盖不当。","pairs":[]}}}}}]},{"id":"section2-part-a-2","kind":"reading","title":"Text 2","textNo":2,"directions":"","points":10,"passage":{"title":"Text 2","paragraphs":[{"id":"p-section2-part-a-2-1","text":"Since the dawn of human ingenuity, people have devised ever more cunning tools to cope with work that is dangerous, boring, burdensome, or just plain nasty. That compulsion has resulted in robotics—the science of conferring various human capabilities on machines. And if scientists have yet to create the mechanical version of science fiction, they have begun to come close."},{"id":"p-section2-part-a-2-2","text":"As a result, the modern world is increasingly populated by intelligent gizmos whose presence we barely notice but whose universal existence has removed much human labor. Our factories hum to the rhythm of robot assembly arms. Our banking is done at automated teller terminals that thank us with mechanical politeness for the transaction. Our subway trains are controlled by tireless robot-drivers. And thanks to the continual miniaturization of electronics and micro-mechanics, there are already robot systems that can perform some kinds of brain and bone surgery with submillimeter accuracy—far greater precision than highly skilled physicians can achieve with their hands alone."},{"id":"p-section2-part-a-2-3","text":"But if robots are to reach the next stage of laborsaving utility, they will have to operate with less human supervision and be able to make at least a few decisions for themselves—goals that pose a real challenge. \"While we know how to tell a robot to handle a specific error,\" says Dave Lavery, manager of a robotics program at NASA, \"we can't yet give a robot enough 'common sense' to reliably interact with a dynamic world.\""},{"id":"p-section2-part-a-2-4","text":"Indeed the quest for true artificial intelligence has produced very mixed results. Despite a spell of initial optimism in the 1960s and 1970s when it appeared that transistor circuits and microprocessors might be able to copy the action of the human brain by the year 2010, researchers lately have begun to extend that forecast by decades if not centuries."},{"id":"p-section2-part-a-2-5","text":"What they found, in attempting to model thought, is that the human brain's roughly one hundred billion nerve cells are much more talented—and human perception far more complicated—than previously imagined. They have built robots that can recognize the error of a machine panel by a fraction of a millimeter in a controlled factory environment. But the human mind can glimpse a rapidly changing scene and immediately disregard the 98 percent that is irrelevant, instantaneously focusing on the monkey at the side of a winding forest road or the single suspicious face in a big crowd. The most advanced computer systems on Earth can't approach that kind of ability, and neuroscientists still don't know quite how we do it."}]},"questions":[{"n":26,"stem":"Human ingenuity was initially demonstrated in____.","options":[{"key":"A","text":"the use of machines to produce science fiction."},{"key":"B","text":"the wide use of machines in manufacturing industry."},{"key":"C","text":"the invention of tools for difficult and dangerous work."},{"key":"D","text":"the elite's cunning tackling of dangerous and boring work."}],"answer":"C","explanation":{"answer":"C","type":"细节题","stemZh":"人类的聪明才智最初体现在____。","choicesZh":{"A":"使用机器来创作科幻小说。","B":"机器在制造业中的广泛使用。","C":"为艰难和危险工作发明工具。","D":"精英阶层巧妙地处理危险和枯燥的工作。"},"analysis":{"type":"Human ingenuity was initially demonstrated in____ 问的是一个具体起源事实，不含 infer/suggest/imply 等推断动词，也不问主旨或态度。","parse":"Human ingenuity was initially demonstrated in____ 是一个被动语态的简单句，主语 Human ingenuity，谓语 was demonstrated，副词 initially 修饰谓语指明时间，空格处由介词 in 引出抽象名词或动名词短语，无陷阱。","locateEn":"Since the dawn of human ingenuity, people have devised ever more cunning tools to cope with work that is dangerous, boring, burdensome, or just plain nasty.","locateZh":"自人类智慧的曙光初现以来，人们就发明了越来越精巧的工具，来应付那些危险的、乏味的、繁重的、或者干脆令人厌恶的工作。","options":{"A":{"flag":"","note":"原文里 science fiction 只是\"科幻里的机械人\"作为参照物，并非人类发明工具的用途；A 把\"用机器制造科幻\"当成 ingenuity 的体现，与原文完全无关。","pairs":[]},"B":{"flag":"","note":"Our factories hum to the rhythm of robot assembly arms 是\"现在工厂广泛使用\"的现状，对应 initially 之后的阶段，不是 ingenuity 最初的体现。","pairs":[]},"C":{"flag":"","note":"C 项把\"造工具\"和\"应付危险/繁重工作\"两要素都保留，且对原文形容词做了合理的上位归并，没有多余信息，与预判完全吻合。","pairs":[{"orig":"devised ever more cunning tools to cope with work that is dangerous, boring, burdensome, or just plain nasty","opt":"the invention of tools for difficult and dangerous work"},{"orig":"tools to cope with work","opt":"tools for…work"}]},"D":{"flag":"","note":"原文主语是 people——泛指人类，而 D 项把它窄化为 the elite's，这是范围偷改；同时漏掉了 burdensome 与 nasty 两类工作，覆盖也不完整。","pairs":[]}}}}},{"n":27,"stem":"The word \"gizmos\" (line 1, paragraph 2) most probably means____.","options":[{"key":"A","text":"programs"},{"key":"B","text":"experts"},{"key":"C","text":"devices"},{"key":"D","text":"creatures"}],"answer":"C","explanation":{"answer":"C","type":"词义句意题","stemZh":"第二段第一行中的\"gizmos\"一词最可能的意思是____。","choicesZh":{"A":"程序","B":"专家","C":"装置","D":"生物"},"analysis":{"type":"The word \"gizmos\" (line 1, paragraph 2) most probably means____ 形式上即\"the word X most probably means\"，是词义题的标志句式。","parse":"The word \"gizmos\" (line 1, paragraph 2) most probably means____ 主语是 the word \"gizmos\"，括号内是位置插入语，谓语 means 之前的 most probably 是程度副词，表示\"最有可能\"，提示答案是上下文推断出的语境义。","locateEn":"As a result, the modern world is increasingly populated by intelligent gizmos whose presence we barely notice but whose universal existence has removed much human labor.","locateZh":"结果，现代世界越来越多地被各种智能\"小玩意\"占据，它们的存在我们几乎察觉不到，但它们的普遍存在已替代了大量人工劳动。","options":{"A":{"flag":"","note":"programs 指软件程序，而段内并列例子 robot assembly arms 等都是\"硬件装置\"，与 programs 不匹配。","pairs":[]},"B":{"flag":"","note":"experts 指人类专家，与原文 intelligent gizmos 的\"机器\"指向完全不同——下文例子全是机器，无任何人类专家在替代人力。","pairs":[]},"C":{"flag":"","note":"段内 gizmos 的所有实例都是\"机器/装置/系统\"，与 devices 完全契合；其余三项无任何例子支撑。","pairs":[{"orig":"intelligent gizmos","opt":"devices"}]},"D":{"flag":"","note":"creatures 一般指有生命的生物，原文 gizmos 显然是机械装置，没有生命属性。","pairs":[]}}}}},{"n":28,"stem":"According to the text, what is beyond man's ability now is to design a robot that can____.","options":[{"key":"A","text":"fulfill delicate tasks like performing brain surgery."},{"key":"B","text":"interact with human beings verbally."},{"key":"C","text":"have a little common sense."},{"key":"D","text":"respond independently to a changing world."}],"answer":"D","explanation":{"answer":"D","type":"细节题","stemZh":"根据文章,现在超出人类能力的是设计一个能够____的机器人。","choicesZh":{"A":"完成像实施脑外科手术这样的精细任务。","B":"与人类进行语言交流。","C":"具有一点常识。","D":"独立地对变化的世界做出反应。"},"analysis":{"type":"what is beyond man's ability now is to design a robot that can____ 在问一个具体的、现在做不到的事，属于事实细节，并非要求多步推断。","parse":"According to the text, what is beyond man's ability now is to design a robot that can____ 主句是 what is beyond man's ability now is to design a robot，what 引导主语从句，is to design 作表语，that can____ 是修饰 robot 的定语从句，空格填动词原形短语。","locateEn":"\"While we know how to tell a robot to handle a specific error,\" says Dave Lavery, manager of a robotics program at NASA, \"we can't yet give a robot enough 'common sense' to reliably interact with a dynamic world.\"","locateZh":"NASA 一个机器人项目的负责人 Dave Lavery 说：\"虽然我们知道怎么让机器人处理某个具体的错误，但我们还无法赋予机器人足够的'常识'，来可靠地与一个动态的世界互动。\"","options":{"A":{"flag":"","note":"there are already robot systems that can perform some kinds of brain and bone surgery with submillimeter accuracy 明示机器人已经能做精细脑外科手术，恰好是\"已实现\"的例子，与题干 beyond man's ability 相反。","pairs":[]},"B":{"flag":"","note":"全文未出现 verbal/speech/language 等任何口头交互讨论；B 项凭空增加了\"用语言与人互动\"的能力维度。","pairs":[]},"C":{"flag":"","note":"原文是 we can't yet give a robot enough 'common sense'——\"不足以充分应对\"，而 C 项 have a little common sense 改为\"哪怕一点都没有\"，量级偏离；事实是机器人能处理具体错误，已具备一定有限\"常识\"。","pairs":[]},"D":{"flag":"","note":"D 把\"自主决策（independently）\"和\"应对变化世界（respond to a changing world）\"两要素合并，与预判完全吻合。","pairs":[{"orig":"reliably interact with a dynamic world","opt":"respond independently to a changing world"},{"orig":"operate with less human supervision and be able to make at least a few decisions for themselves","opt":"respond independently"}]}}}}},{"n":29,"stem":"Besides reducing human labor, robots can also____.","options":[{"key":"A","text":"make a few decisions for themselves."},{"key":"B","text":"deal with some errors with human intervention."},{"key":"C","text":"improve factory environments."},{"key":"D","text":"cultivate human creativity."}],"answer":"B","explanation":{"answer":"B","type":"细节题","stemZh":"除了减少人类劳动,机器人还可以____。","choicesZh":{"A":"为自己做一些决定。","B":"在人类干预下处理一些错误。","C":"改善工厂环境。","D":"培养人类的创造力。"},"analysis":{"type":"Besides reducing human labor, robots can also____ 形式上是补充一个并列事实，不涉及推断或主旨。","parse":"Besides reducing human labor, robots can also____ Besides 引导介词短语作状语，提示\"除…之外\"；主句主语 robots、谓语 can also，空格处填动词原形短语；注意 Besides 表\"另加\"而非\"除掉\"。","locateEn":"\"While we know how to tell a robot to handle a specific error,\" says Dave Lavery, manager of a robotics program at NASA, \"we can't yet give a robot enough 'common sense' to reliably interact with a dynamic world.\"","locateZh":"NASA 一个机器人项目负责人 Dave Lavery 说：\"虽然我们知道怎么让机器人处理某个具体的错误，但我们还无法赋予它足够的'常识'，来可靠地与动态世界互动。\"","options":{"A":{"flag":"","note":"if robots are to reach the next stage of laborsaving utility, they will have to…be able to make at least a few decisions for themselves 是未来条件下的目标（will have to），不是机器人当下已具备的能力；选 A 就把\"想达到\"当作\"已具备\"。","pairs":[]},"B":{"flag":"","note":"B 没有夸大机器人能力，把\"人参与\"这一原文限定完整保留下来，与预判一致。","pairs":[{"orig":"we know how to tell a robot to handle a specific error","opt":"deal with some errors with human intervention"}]},"C":{"flag":"","note":"in a controlled factory environment 只是机器人识别误差的工作场景，不是机器人改善工厂环境的能力。","pairs":[]},"D":{"flag":"","note":"全文未提机器人能培养人的创造力；该能力是凭空捏造。","pairs":[]}}}}},{"n":30,"stem":"The author uses the example of a monkey to argue that robots are____.","options":[{"key":"A","text":"expected to copy human brain in internal structure."},{"key":"B","text":"able to perceive abnormalities immediately."},{"key":"C","text":"far less able than human brain in focusing on relevant information."},{"key":"D","text":"best used in a controlled environment."}],"answer":"C","explanation":{"answer":"C","type":"例证目的题","stemZh":"作者用猴子的例子来论证机器人____。","choicesZh":{"A":"被期望在内部结构上复制人脑。","B":"能够立即察觉异常。","C":"在聚焦相关信息方面远不如人脑。","D":"最适合在受控环境中使用。"},"analysis":{"type":"The author uses the example of a monkey to argue that robots are____ 句式即\"uses the example of X to argue that…\"，是例证目的题的典型形式。","parse":"The author uses the example of a monkey to argue that robots are____ 主语 The author，谓语 uses，宾语 the example of a monkey，to argue that… 是不定式作目的状语，that 引导的是 argue 的宾语从句，空格在从句表语位置，填形容词性短语。","locateEn":"But the human mind can glimpse a rapidly changing scene and immediately disregard the 98 percent that is irrelevant, instantaneously focusing on the monkey at the side of a winding forest road or the single suspicious face in a big crowd. The most advanced computer systems on Earth can't approach that kind of ability, and neuroscientists still don't know quite how we do it.","locateZh":"但人脑能瞥一眼飞速变化的场景，瞬间过滤掉 98% 的无关信息，迅速聚焦于林间弯路边的猴子，或人群中那张可疑面孔。地球上最先进的电脑系统都无法接近这种能力，神经科学家至今也不太清楚我们是怎么做到的。","options":{"A":{"flag":"","note":"原文谈的是\"能力不及\"，并未要求机器人在\"内部结构\"上复制人脑；transistor circuits and microprocessors might be able to copy the action of the human brain 用的是 action（功能），不是 internal structure（结构）。","pairs":[]},"B":{"flag":"","note":"原文谈的是从场景中聚焦\"相关信息\"（猴子、可疑面孔），而 abnormalities（异常）并非原文措辞，且把\"相关\"窄化为\"异常\"；且 B 把这种能力归给了机器人本身，与原文\"人脑\"主语颠倒。","pairs":[]},"C":{"flag":"","note":"C 把论点\"电脑赶不上人脑\"翻译为\"在聚焦相关信息这件事上远不如人脑\"，并保留\"相关信息\"这一关键限定，与预判完全吻合。","pairs":[{"orig":"The most advanced computer systems on Earth can't approach that kind of ability","opt":"far less able than human brain in focusing on relevant information"},{"orig":"disregard the 98 percent that is irrelevant, instantaneously focusing on the monkey…or the single suspicious face","opt":"focusing on relevant information"}]},"D":{"flag":"","note":"They have built robots that can recognize the error of a machine panel by a fraction of a millimeter in a controlled factory environment. 是另一句独立陈述，monkey 例子要支撑的不是\"机器人最好在受控环境用\"，而是\"机器人在动态场景中不如人脑\"。","pairs":[]}}}}}]},{"id":"section2-part-a-3","kind":"reading","title":"Text 3","textNo":3,"directions":"","points":10,"passage":{"title":"Text 3","paragraphs":[{"id":"p-section2-part-a-3-1","text":"Could the bad old days of economic decline be about to return? Since OPEC agreed to supply-cuts in March, the price of crude oil has jumped to almost $26 a barrel, up from less than $10 last December. This near-tripling of oil prices calls up scary memories of the 1973 oil shock, when prices quadrupled, and 1979-1980, when they also almost tripled. Both previous shocks resulted in double-digit inflation and global economic decline. So where are the headlines warning of gloom and doom this time?"},{"id":"p-section2-part-a-3-2","text":"The oil price was given another push up this week when Iraq suspended oil exports. Strengthening economic growth, at the same time as winter grips the northern hemisphere, could push the price higher still in the short term."},{"id":"p-section2-part-a-3-3","text":"Yet there are good reasons to expect the economic consequences now to be less severe than in the 1970s. In most countries the cost of crude oil now accounts for a smaller share of the price of petrol than it did in the 1970s. In Europe, taxes account for up to four-fifths of the retail price, so even quite big changes in the price of crude have a more muted effect on pump prices than in the past."},{"id":"p-section2-part-a-3-4","text":"Rich economies are also less dependent on oil than they were, and so less sensitive to swings in the oil price. Energy conservation, a shift to other fuels and a decline in the importance of heavy, energy-intensive industries have reduced oil consumption. Software, consultancy and mobile telephones use far less oil than steel or car production. For each dollar of GDP (in constant prices) rich economies now use nearly 50% less oil than in 1973. The OECD estimates in its latest Economic Outlook that, if oil prices averaged $22 a barrel for a full year, compared with $13 in 1998, this would increase the oil import bill in rich economies by only 0.25-0.5% of GDP. That is less than one-quarter of the income loss in 1974 or 1980. On the other hand, oil-importing emerging economies—to which heavy industry has shifted—have become more energy-intensive, and so could be more seriously squeezed."},{"id":"p-section2-part-a-3-5","text":"One more reason not to lose sleep over the rise in oil prices is that, unlike the rises in the 1970s, it has not occurred against the background of general commodity-price inflation and global excess demand. A sizable portion of the world is only just emerging from economic decline. The Economist's commodity price index is broadly unchanging from a year ago. In 1973 commodity prices jumped by 70%, and in 1979 by almost 30%."}]},"questions":[{"n":31,"stem":"The main reason for the latest rise of oil price is____","options":[{"key":"A","text":"global inflation."},{"key":"B","text":"reduction in supply."},{"key":"C","text":"fast growth in economy."},{"key":"D","text":"Iraq's suspension of exports."}],"answer":"B","explanation":{"answer":"B","type":"细节题","stemZh":"石油价格最近上涨的主要原因是____","choicesZh":{"A":"全球通货膨胀。","B":"供应减少。","C":"经济快速增长。","D":"伊拉克暂停出口。"},"analysis":{"type":"The main reason for the latest rise of oil price is 是问一个具体的客观事实——「这次油价涨是为啥」，没有 infer/imply 等推断词，故为细节题。","parse":"The main reason for the latest rise of oil price is 是一个不完整陈述句，主语 The main reason，for 引导后置定语限定 reason，is 后接选项。结构平铺直叙，无陷阱。","locateEn":"Since OPEC agreed to supply-cuts in March, the price of crude oil has jumped to almost $26 a barrel, up from less than $10 last December.","locateZh":"自从 OPEC 在三月份同意减产以来，原油价格已从去年 12 月的不到 10 美元/桶飙升到了将近 26 美元/桶。","options":{"A":{"flag":"","note":"global inflation 在全文从未被列为「这次油价上涨的原因」；相反 it has not occurred against the background of general commodity-price inflation 明确说这次没有大宗商品通胀背景。","pairs":[]},"B":{"flag":"","note":"预判答案是「供应减少」，reduction in supply 与之逐字对应，是 supply-cuts 的标准名词化改写，故选 B。","pairs":[{"orig":"OPEC agreed to supply-cuts","opt":"reduction in supply"}]},"C":{"flag":"","note":"Strengthening economic growth, at the same time as winter grips the northern hemisphere, could push the price higher still in the short term 显示经济增长只是短期里「可能再推高」的力量，而非这次上涨的主因；主因仍是 OPEC agreed to supply-cuts。","pairs":[]},"D":{"flag":"","note":"The oil price was given another push up this week when Iraq suspended oil exports 中 another push up 一词点明 Iraq 暂停出口只是「又一记推力」，并非「主」因；主因依然是 OPEC agreed to supply-cuts。","pairs":[]}}}}},{"n":32,"stem":"It can be inferred from the text that the retail price of petrol will go up dramatically if____.","options":[{"key":"A","text":"price of crude rises."},{"key":"B","text":"commodity prices rise."},{"key":"C","text":"consumption rises."},{"key":"D","text":"oil taxes rise."}],"answer":"D","explanation":{"answer":"D","type":"推断题","stemZh":"从文中可以推断,如果____,汽油零售价格将会大幅上涨。","choicesZh":{"A":"原油价格上涨。","B":"商品价格上涨。","C":"消费增加。","D":"石油税上涨。"},"analysis":{"type":"It can be inferred from the text 直接出现 inferred，说明答案不会在原文逐字写出，而要从原文事实做一步逻辑延伸。","parse":"It can be inferred from the text that the retail price of petrol will go up dramatically if 主句 It can be inferred…，that 引导宾语从句，从句里 if 引导条件状语从句、其内容被切到选项里。考生易把 if 漏掉，请明确：选哪个，就意味着「哪个条件成立时」petrol 价才会大涨。","locateEn":"In Europe, taxes account for up to four-fifths of the retail price, so even quite big changes in the price of crude have a more muted effect on pump prices than in the past.","locateZh":"在欧洲，税收占了零售价的至多 4/5，因此即便原油价格发生相当大的变化，对加油站零售价的影响也比过去更被削弱。","options":{"A":{"flag":"","note":"even quite big changes in the price of crude have a more muted effect on pump prices than in the past 明说原油「再大涨」也只是 muted effect（被削弱的影响），不可能让 retail dramatically 上涨。","pairs":[]},"B":{"flag":"","note":"P3 讨论的是 taxes ↔ crude oil ↔ retail 三者，未把 commodity prices 纳入到「让 retail dramatically 涨」的链条；P5 提到 commodity-price inflation 只是在说宏观背景，与 retail of petrol 无直接因果。","pairs":[]},"C":{"flag":"","note":"全文未把 consumption rises 与 retail price dramatically 直接挂钩；rich economies now use nearly 50% less oil than in 1973 反而强调富国消费下降，使 retail 对油价不敏感。","pairs":[]},"D":{"flag":"","note":"预判「动税才会让零售价大涨」，oil taxes rise 把这个反向推一步翻成 if 条件，与预判精确对应，故选 D。","pairs":[{"orig":"taxes account for up to four-fifths of the retail price","opt":"oil taxes rise"}]}}}}},{"n":33,"stem":"The estimates in Economic Outlook show that in rich countries____.","options":[{"key":"A","text":"heavy industry becomes more energy-intensive."},{"key":"B","text":"income loss mainly results from fluctuating crude oil prices."},{"key":"C","text":"manufacturing industry has been seriously squeezed."},{"key":"D","text":"oil price changes have no significant impact on GDP."}],"answer":"D","explanation":{"answer":"D","type":"细节题","stemZh":"《经济展望》中的估算表明,在富裕国家____。","choicesZh":{"A":"重工业变得更加能源密集。","B":"收入损失主要源于原油价格波动。","C":"制造业受到严重挤压。","D":"石油价格变化对GDP没有显著影响。"},"analysis":{"type":"The estimates in Economic Outlook show that 直接问该报告 show 出什么客观结论，没有推断词，是典型细节题。","parse":"The estimates in Economic Outlook show that in rich countries 主语 The estimates，介词短语 in Economic Outlook 修饰 estimates，show 后 that 引导宾语从句，in rich countries 又是从句里的地点状语。结构稍长但无逻辑陷阱。","locateEn":"The OECD estimates in its latest Economic Outlook that, if oil prices averaged $22 a barrel for a full year, compared with $13 in 1998, this would increase the oil import bill in rich economies by only 0.25-0.5% of GDP.","locateZh":"OECD 在其最新一期《经济展望》中估计，若油价全年均价为 22 美元/桶（相比 1998 年的 13 美元），富国的石油进口账单也只会因此上升 GDP 的 0.25%-0.5%。","options":{"A":{"flag":"","note":"oil-importing emerging economies—to which heavy industry has shifted—have become more energy-intensive 明确说「重工业更密集」的是 emerging economies，不是 Q33 所问的 rich countries。","pairs":[]},"B":{"flag":"","note":"That is less than one-quarter of the income loss in 1974 or 1980 里的 income loss 是 1974/1980 那两次大事件的损失，且只用作量级对比；原文未说富国当前的 income loss「主要源于」原油价波动。","pairs":[]},"C":{"flag":"","note":"oil-importing emerging economies—to which heavy industry has shifted—…could be more seriously squeezed 中被 seriously squeezed 的是 emerging economies，不是 rich countries 的 manufacturing industry。","pairs":[]},"D":{"flag":"","note":"预判是「影响极小」，oil price changes have no significant impact on GDP 用含蓄否定把极小程度直接表述为「无显著影响」，与预判逐字对齐。","pairs":[{"orig":"this would increase the oil import bill in rich economies by only 0.25-0.5% of GDP","opt":"oil price changes have no significant impact on GDP"}]}}}}},{"n":34,"stem":"We can draw a conclusion from the text that____.","options":[{"key":"A","text":"oil-price shocks are less shocking now."},{"key":"B","text":"inflation seems irrelevant to oil-price shocks."},{"key":"C","text":"energy conservation can keep down the oil prices."},{"key":"D","text":"the price rise of crude leads to the shrinking of heavy industry."}],"answer":"A","explanation":{"answer":"A","type":"主旨题","stemZh":"我们可以从文中得出结论____。","choicesZh":{"A":"石油价格冲击现在没那么令人震惊了。","B":"通货膨胀似乎与石油价格冲击无关。","C":"节约能源可以抑制石油价格。","D":"原油价格上涨导致重工业萎缩。"},"analysis":{"type":"We can draw a conclusion from the text that 没有任何具体的定位抓手，问的是「从整篇文章能得出的结论」，按主旨题路径处理。","parse":"We can draw a conclusion from the text that 主句 We can draw a conclusion，from the text 是状语，that 引导同位语从句解释 conclusion 的内容。结构清晰、无陷阱。","locateEn":"","locateZh":"","options":{"A":{"flag":"","note":"预判是「这次冲击没那么猛」，oil-price shocks are less shocking now 把它直接翻成同义判断，且 P3P4P5 三段都可逐一为它背书，故选 A。","pairs":[{"orig":"there are good reasons to expect the economic consequences now to be less severe than in the 1970s","opt":"oil-price shocks are less shocking now"},{"orig":"One more reason not to lose sleep over the rise in oil prices","opt":"oil-price shocks are less shocking now"}]},"B":{"flag":"","note":"Both previous shocks resulted in double-digit inflation and global economic decline 反而承认了油价与通胀的历史关联；全文只是说「这次背景不同」，并未得出 inflation irrelevant 这种全称否定的结论。","pairs":[]},"C":{"flag":"","note":"Energy conservation, a shift to other fuels and a decline in the importance of heavy, energy-intensive industries have reduced oil consumption 只说节能降低了「消费量」、从而让经济对油价波动更不敏感，并不等于节能能「压低油价本身」。","pairs":[]},"D":{"flag":"","note":"a decline in the importance of heavy, energy-intensive industries 是富国经济结构演变的结果；oil-importing emerging economies—to which heavy industry has shifted 也表明重工业是「转移」而非「萎缩」。原文未把原油价上涨当作重工业萎缩的原因。","pairs":[]}}}}},{"n":35,"stem":"From the text we can see that the writer seems____.","options":[{"key":"A","text":"optimistic."},{"key":"B","text":"sensitive."},{"key":"C","text":"gloomy."},{"key":"D","text":"scared."}],"answer":"A","explanation":{"answer":"A","type":"态度题","stemZh":"从文中可以看出作者似乎____。","choicesZh":{"A":"乐观。","B":"敏感。","C":"悲观。","D":"恐惧。"},"analysis":{"type":"From the text we can see that the writer seems 不问内容、只问 writer seems 是怎样的，正是态度题的典型问法。","parse":"From the text we can see that the writer seems 主句 we can see，that 引导宾语从句，from the text 为状语。结构平铺直叙，无陷阱。","locateEn":"","locateZh":"","options":{"A":{"flag":"","note":"预判作者「偏乐观、不担心」，四个选项里只有 optimistic 是正向极性，故选 A。","pairs":[{"orig":"there are good reasons to expect the economic consequences now to be less severe than in the 1970s","opt":"optimistic"},{"orig":"not to lose sleep over the rise in oil prices","opt":"optimistic"}]},"B":{"flag":"","note":"sensitive 指「敏感的」，原文 less sensitive to swings in the oil price 是描述「富国经济对油价的敏感度」，并非作者本人的态度；态度题不能拿原文里描述别人/别物的词来贴作者。","pairs":[]},"C":{"flag":"","note":"gloomy 是负向，意为「悲观」；而原文 So where are the headlines warning of gloom and doom this time? 是在反问「这次怎么不见悲观头条」，恰恰否定了 gloomy 的态度。","pairs":[]},"D":{"flag":"","note":"This near-tripling of oil prices calls up scary memories of the 1973 oil shock 中的 scary 是描写「旧记忆」，作者立刻在 Yet there are good reasons to expect… 用 Yet 转折反驳这种 scared 情绪；全文走向恰恰是「不必怕」。","pairs":[]}}}}}]},{"id":"section2-part-a-4","kind":"reading","title":"Text 4","textNo":4,"directions":"","points":10,"passage":{"title":"Text 4","paragraphs":[{"id":"p-section2-part-a-4-1","text":"The Supreme Court's decisions on physician-assisted suicide carry important implications for how medicine seeks to relieve dying patients of pain and suffering."},{"id":"p-section2-part-a-4-2","text":"Although it ruled that there is no constitutional right to physician-assisted suicide, the Court in effect supported the medical principle of \"double effect\", a centuries-old moral principle holding that an action having two effects—a good one that is intended and a harmful one that is foreseen—is permissible if the actor intends only the good effect."},{"id":"p-section2-part-a-4-3","text":"Doctors have used that principle in recent years to justify using high doses of morphine to control terminally ill patients' pain, even though increasing dosages will eventually kill the patient."},{"id":"p-section2-part-a-4-4","text":"Nancy Dubler, director of Montefiore Medical Center, contends that the principle will shield doctors who \"until now have very, very strongly insisted that they could not give patients sufficient medication to control their pain if that might hasten death\"."},{"id":"p-section2-part-a-4-5","text":"George Annas, chair of the health law department at Boston University, maintains that, as long as a doctor prescribes a drug for a legitimate medical purpose, the doctor has done nothing illegal even if the patient uses the drug to hasten death. \"It's like surgery,\" he says. \"We don't call those deaths homicides because the doctors didn't intend to kill their patients, although they risked their death. If you're a physician, you can risk your patient's suicide as long as you don't intend their suicide.\""},{"id":"p-section2-part-a-4-6","text":"On another level, many in the medical community acknowledge that the assisted-suicide debate has been fueled in part by the despair of patients for whom modern medicine has prolonged the physical agony of dying."},{"id":"p-section2-part-a-4-7","text":"Just three weeks before the Court's ruling on physician-assisted suicide, the National Academy of Science (NAS) released a two-volume report, Approaching Death: Improving Care at the End of Life. It identifies the undertreatment of pain and the aggressive use of \"ineffectual and forced medical procedures that may prolong and even dishonor the period of dying\" as the twin problems of end-of-life care."},{"id":"p-section2-part-a-4-8","text":"The profession is taking steps to require young doctors to train in hospices, to test knowledge of aggressive pain management therapies, to develop a Medicare billing code for hospital-based care, and to develop new standards for assessing and treating pain at the end of life."},{"id":"p-section2-part-a-4-9","text":"Annas says lawyers can play a key role in insisting that these well-meaning medical initiatives translate into better care. \"Large numbers of physicians seem unconcerned with the pain their patients are needlessly and predictably suffering\", to the extent that it constitutes \"systematic patient abuse\". He says medical licensing boards \"must make it clear…that painful deaths are presumptively ones that are incompetently managed and should result in license suspension\"."}]},"questions":[{"n":36,"stem":"From the first three paragraphs, we learn that____.","options":[{"key":"A","text":"doctors used to increase drug dosages to control their patients' pain"},{"key":"B","text":"it is still illegal for doctors to help the dying end their lives"},{"key":"C","text":"the Supreme Court strongly opposes physician-assisted suicide"},{"key":"D","text":"patients have no constitutional right to commit suicide"}],"answer":"B","explanation":{"answer":"B","type":"细节题","stemZh":"从前三段我们可以得知____。","choicesZh":{"A":"医生过去常常增加药物剂量来控制病人的疼痛","B":"医生帮助临终病人结束生命仍然是非法的","C":"最高法院强烈反对医生协助自杀","D":"病人没有宪法规定的自杀权利"},"analysis":{"type":"题干 From the first three paragraphs, we learn that 仅要求我们从前三段读出事实，没有 infer/imply/suggest 等推断信号。","parse":"From the first three paragraphs, we learn that____ 是 we learn that 引导的省略宾语从句，从句内容由四个选项补完；From … 状语限定证据来源，结构平铺直叙，无陷阱。","locateEn":"Although it ruled that there is no constitutional right to physician-assisted suicide, the Court in effect supported the medical principle of \"double effect\".","locateZh":"尽管最高法院裁定不存在医师协助自杀的宪法权利，但事实上它支持了医学上的'双重效应'原则。","options":{"A":{"flag":"","note":"doctors used to increase drug dosages to control their patients' pain 中 used to 暗示'过去常做、现在不做'；而 Doctors have used that principle in recent years 用现在完成时表明该做法延续至今，A 把时态偷换成'过去时'，与原文相反。","pairs":[]},"B":{"flag":"","note":"预判已得'协助自杀在法律上不被允许'，选项 it is still illegal for doctors to help the dying end their lives 与之直接对应，故锁定 B。","pairs":[{"orig":"there is no constitutional right to physician-assisted suicide","opt":"it is still illegal for doctors to help the dying end their lives"},{"orig":"Doctors have used that principle in recent years to justify using high doses of morphine","opt":"it is still illegal for doctors to help the dying end their lives"}]},"C":{"flag":"","note":"the Supreme Court strongly opposes physician-assisted suicide 用 strongly opposes 把法院的态度推到'强烈反对'；原文 in effect supported the medical principle of \"double effect\" 显示法院实际上反而'有限支持'双重效应原则，对协助自杀本身只是不立宪法权，没有'强烈反对'。","pairs":[]},"D":{"flag":"","note":"patients have no constitutional right to commit suicide 把宪法权范围扩展到一般 commit suicide；原文 no constitutional right to physician-assisted suicide 只说没有'医师协助自杀'的宪法权利，而非'自杀'本身没有宪法权。","pairs":[]}}}}},{"n":37,"stem":"Which of the following statements is true according to the text?","options":[{"key":"A","text":"Doctors will be held guilty if they risk their patients' death."},{"key":"B","text":"Modern medicine has assisted terminally ill patients in painless recovery."},{"key":"C","text":"The Court ruled that high-dosage pain-relieving medication can be prescribed."},{"key":"D","text":"A doctor's medication is no longer justified by his intentions."}],"answer":"C","explanation":{"answer":"C","type":"细节题","stemZh":"根据原文,下列哪项陈述是正确的?","choicesZh":{"A":"如果医生使病人面临死亡风险,他们将被判有罪。","B":"现代医学已帮助晚期病人实现无痛康复。","C":"法院裁定可以开具高剂量的止痛药物。","D":"医生的用药不再以其意图作为正当理由。"},"analysis":{"type":"题干 Which of the following statements is true according to the text 要求判断哪个陈述与原文相符，本质是逐项核对事实。","parse":"Which of the following statements is true according to the text? 是 which 引导的特殊疑问句，主语 Which of the following statements，谓语 is true，状语 according to the text 限定判断依据；结构清晰，无陷阱。","locateEn":"Doctors have used that principle in recent years to justify using high doses of morphine to control terminally ill patients' pain, even though increasing dosages will eventually kill the patient.","locateZh":"近年来，医生们一直援引该原则为自己辩护——使用大剂量吗啡来控制末期病人的疼痛，即便增加剂量最终会导致病人死亡。","options":{"A":{"flag":"","note":"Doctors will be held guilty if they risk their patients' death 与 Annas 主张 If you're a physician, you can risk your patient's suicide as long as you don't intend their suicide 正好相反——只要不蓄意促死，承担'死亡风险'本身不构成罪责。","pairs":[]},"B":{"flag":"","note":"Modern medicine has assisted terminally ill patients in painless recovery 说现代医学帮助末期病人'无痛康复'；原文 modern medicine has prolonged the physical agony of dying 恰恰是相反：现代医学延长了濒死的肉体痛苦。","pairs":[]},"C":{"flag":"","note":"Q37 答案必须由原文直接支撑：原文显示法院支持的'双重效应'原则正是为大剂量止痛背书，故 C 与原文事实一致。","pairs":[{"orig":"the Court in effect supported the medical principle of \"double effect\"","opt":"the Court ruled that high-dosage pain-relieving medication can be prescribed"},{"orig":"Doctors have used that principle in recent years to justify using high doses of morphine to control terminally ill patients' pain","opt":"the Court ruled that high-dosage pain-relieving medication can be prescribed"}]},"D":{"flag":"","note":"A doctor's medication is no longer justified by his intentions 说医师用药'不再'由意图证成；原文 the Court in effect supported the medical principle of \"double effect\" 与 as long as a doctor prescribes a drug for a legitimate medical purpose, the doctor has done nothing illegal 都强调'意图'仍是关键证成因素。","pairs":[]}}}}},{"n":38,"stem":"According to the NAS's report, one of the problems in end-of-life care is____.","options":[{"key":"A","text":"prolonged medical procedures"},{"key":"B","text":"inadequate treatment of pain"},{"key":"C","text":"systematic drug abuse"},{"key":"D","text":"insufficient hospital care"}],"answer":"B","explanation":{"answer":"B","type":"细节题","stemZh":"根据NAS的报告,临终关怀中的问题之一是____。","choicesZh":{"A":"prolonged medical procedures","B":"疼痛治疗不充分","C":"系统性药物滥用","D":"医院护理不足"},"analysis":{"type":"题干 According to the NAS's report, one of the problems in end-of-life care is 明确锁定 NAS 报告内容，问其中一个具体问题。","parse":"According to the NAS's report, one of the problems in end-of-life care is____ 主干 one of the problems … is ___，主语含 of 修饰，谓语简单 is，提示选项与 problems 在语义上同位，需选一个 problem。","locateEn":"It identifies the undertreatment of pain and the aggressive use of \"ineffectual and forced medical procedures that may prolong and even dishonor the period of dying\" as the twin problems of end-of-life care.","locateZh":"该报告指出疼痛治疗不足以及激进使用'可能延长甚至玷污濒死阶段的无效且强加的医疗手段'，是临终关怀的两大问题。","options":{"A":{"flag":"","note":"prolonged medical procedures 只保留了 prolong 的语义，丢掉原文 ineffectual and forced 这两个核心定语；NAS 批评的不是'医疗程序时间长'本身，而是'无效且强加'的程序，A 把范围扩大到所有'被延长的医疗程序'。","pairs":[]},"B":{"flag":"","note":"预判的两条问题里第一条'疼痛治疗不足'被 B 项原样替换，故锁定 B。","pairs":[{"orig":"the undertreatment of pain","opt":"inadequate treatment of pain"}]},"C":{"flag":"","note":"systematic drug abuse 谈的是'系统性滥用药物'；NAS 报告并未把'药物滥用'列入两大问题，原文整段也没出现 drug abuse 这一概念，属凭空捏造。","pairs":[]},"D":{"flag":"","note":"insufficient hospital care 改成'医院护理不足'；原文 NAS 报告说的是'对疼痛治疗不足'与'激进医疗手段过度'，并未指控医院护理总量不够，D 把焦点从治疗质量/手段偏移到护理数量。","pairs":[]}}}}},{"n":39,"stem":"Which of the following best defines the word \"aggressive\" (line 4, paragraph 7)?","options":[{"key":"A","text":"Bold."},{"key":"B","text":"Harmful."},{"key":"C","text":"Careless."},{"key":"D","text":"Desperate."}],"answer":"A","explanation":{"answer":"A","type":"词义句意题","stemZh":"下列哪项最准确地定义了第7段第4行中的词语aggressive?","choicesZh":{"A":"大胆的。","B":"有害的。","C":"粗心的。","D":"绝望的。"},"analysis":{"type":"题干 Which of the following best defines the word \"aggressive\" (line 4, paragraph 7) 含 best defines 与 line/paragraph 标注，是典型词义题。","parse":"Which of the following best defines the word \"aggressive\" (line 4, paragraph 7)? which 引导的疑问句，谓语 defines，宾语 the word aggressive；括号内是定位提示而非句法成分。","locateEn":"It identifies the undertreatment of pain and the aggressive use of \"ineffectual and forced medical procedures that may prolong and even dishonor the period of dying\" as the twin problems of end-of-life care.","locateZh":"该报告指出疼痛治疗不足以及激进使用'可能延长甚至玷污濒死阶段的无效且强加的医疗手段'，是临终关怀的两大问题。","options":{"A":{"flag":"","note":"P7 的语境批评的是被 aggressive 修饰的对象本身（无效且强加的手段），P8 的语境正面看待 aggressive 镇痛——两处共指向 Bold（大胆/进取），故选 A。","pairs":[{"orig":"aggressive pain management therapies","opt":"Bold."},{"orig":"the aggressive use of \"ineffectual and forced medical procedures\"","opt":"Bold."}]},"B":{"flag":"","note":"Harmful 把整句的负面色彩归到 aggressive 头上；实则 P7 的负义来自 ineffectual and forced，而 aggressive 在 aggressive pain management therapies 是被推广的正面用法，并非天生有害。","pairs":[]},"C":{"flag":"","note":"Careless 暗示'草率、不上心'；而 aggressive 强调'主动而强力'，与 careless 在动机维度上相反——aggressive 的医生反而过度上心、行动过猛，不是不上心。","pairs":[]},"D":{"flag":"","note":"Desperate 含'绝望、走投无路'的情绪色彩；aggressive 描述的是医生主动选择强力手段，并非走投无路被迫为之，情绪维度不匹配。","pairs":[]}}}}},{"n":40,"stem":"George Annas would probably agree that doctors should be punished if they____.","options":[{"key":"A","text":"manage their patients incompetently"},{"key":"B","text":"give patients more medicine than needed"},{"key":"C","text":"reduce drug dosages for their patients"},{"key":"D","text":"prolong the needless suffering of the patients"}],"answer":"D","explanation":{"answer":"D","type":"推断题","stemZh":"George Annas可能会同意,如果医生____,就应当受到惩罚。","choicesZh":{"A":"对病人的管理不称职","B":"给病人的药物超过所需剂量","C":"减少病人的药物剂量","D":"延长病人不必要的痛苦"},"analysis":{"type":"题干 George Annas would probably agree that doctors should be punished if they 含 would probably agree，是典型推断题信号。","parse":"George Annas would probably agree that doctors should be punished if they____ 主句 George Annas would probably agree that…，that 宾从内含 if 条件状语从句，从句由选项补完；情态 would 与 probably 双重弱化，提示这是推断而非细节。","locateEn":"He says medical licensing boards \"must make it clear…that painful deaths are presumptively ones that are incompetently managed and should result in license suspension\".","locateZh":"他说医师执照委员会'必须明示……痛苦的死亡通常意味着处置无能，应导致执照吊销'。","options":{"A":{"flag":"","note":"manage their patients incompetently 看似来自 incompetently managed，但原文是 painful deaths 推出 incompetently managed 这一'反向推定'；A 把'痛苦死亡的诊断结果'当作'应受罚的行为'，把症状当成原因。","pairs":[]},"B":{"flag":"","note":"give patients more medicine than needed 主张'用药过量应受罚'；Annas 在 P5 明确认为只要意图正当，开药即便加速死亡也无违法，他反对的是'用药不足'而非'用药过多'。","pairs":[]},"C":{"flag":"","note":"reduce drug dosages for their patients 主张'减少药量应受罚'听似与 Annas 想法接近，但他反对的是'减剂量'造成病人受苦还是'让病人持续受苦本身'——Annas 主张 painful deaths … should result in license suspension，落点在结果上的痛苦，而 C 把焦点放在剂量这一过程行为上，且原文未直接如此表述。","pairs":[]},"D":{"flag":"","note":"Annas 反复强调让本可避免的疼痛持续下去构成'systematic patient abuse'并应吊销执照，这正是 D 项 prolong the needless suffering 的直接对应。","pairs":[{"orig":"Large numbers of physicians seem unconcerned with the pain their patients are needlessly and predictably suffering","opt":"prolong the needless suffering of the patients"},{"orig":"painful deaths are presumptively ones that are incompetently managed and should result in license suspension","opt":"prolong the needless suffering of the patients"}]}}}}}]},{"id":"section2-part-b","kind":"translation","title":"Section II Part C 英译汉","directions":"Directions: Read the following text carefully and then translate the underlined segments into Chinese. Write your answers on the ANSWER SHEET. ( 10 points)","points":10,"passage":{"paragraphs":[{"id":"p-section2-part-b-1","text":"Almost all our major problems involve human behavior, and they cannot be solved by physical and biological technology alone. What is needed is a technology of behavior, but we have been slow to develop the science from which such a technology might be drawn. (41) One difficulty is that almost all of what is called behavioral science continues to trace behavior to states of mind, feelings, traits of character, human nature, and so on. Physics and biology once followed similar practices and advanced only when they discarded them. (42) The behavioral sciences have been slow to change partly because the explanatory items often seem to be directly observed and partly because other kinds of explanations have been hard to find. The environment is obviously important, but its role has remained obscure. It does not push or pull, it selects, and this function is difficult to discover and analyze. (43) The role of natural selection in evolution was formulated only a little more than a hundred years ago, and the selective role of the environment in shaping and maintaining the behavior of the individual is only beginning to be recognized and studied. As the interaction between organism and environment has come to be understood, however, effects once assigned to states of mind, feelings, and traits are beginning to be traced to accessible conditions, and a technology of behavior may therefore become available. It will not solve our problems, however, until it replaces traditional prescientific views, and these are strongly entrenched. Freedom and dignity illustrate the difficulty. (44) They are the possessions of the autonomous(self-governing) man of traditional theory, and they are essential to practices in which a person is held responsible for his conduct and given credit for his achievements. A scientific analysis shifts both the responsibility and the achievement to the environment. It also raises questions concerning \"values\". Who will use a technology and to what ends? (45) Until these issues are resolved, a technology of behavior will continue to be rejected, and with it possibly the only way to solve our problems."}]},"sentences":[{"n":41,"en":"One difficulty is that almost all of what is called behavioral science continues to trace behavior to states of mind, feelings, traits of character, human nature, and so on.","refZh":"困难之一在于，几乎所有所谓的行为科学依旧把行为归因于心理状态、感受、性格特征、人性等等。","analysis":"","chunks":[{"en":"One difficulty is that","lit":"一个困难是","role":"（主干主谓 + that 宾语从句引导）","note":""},{"en":"almost all of what is called behavioral science","lit":"几乎所有被称为行为科学的东西","role":"（宾语从句主语（含 what 引导的名词性从句））","note":"难点： what is called X = 所谓的 X almost all of what is called behavioral science 这个 what 从句是固定套路：what is called X 就译成「所谓的 X」，比直译「被称作 X 的东西」更地道。almost all of 不要漏译「几乎全部」，它是采分点的程度词。"},{"en":"continues to trace behavior to","lit":"继续把行为追溯到","role":"（宾语从句谓语 + 动词短语）","note":"难点： trace A to B = 把 A 追溯到 B / 把 A 归因于 B trace…to… 是固定搭配，主体考生容易只译「追踪」漏掉「to」的「归因」义。结合上下文 Physics and biology once followed similar practices and advanced only when they discarded them.（作者把这种做法视为该被抛弃的旧路），此处的「追溯到」其实就是「归因于」——译成「将行为归因于」更贴主旨。continues to 的「仍然、依旧」也要译出，是态度词。"},{"en":"states of mind, feelings, traits of character, human nature, and so on.","lit":"心理状态、感受、性格特征、人性等等","role":"（trace…to 的并列宾语）","note":"难点： 并列名词的术语化译法 states of mind 不要硬译「心智的状态」，规范译法是「心理状态/心态」；traits of character 是「性格特征」（不是「品格痕迹」）；human nature 是「人性」（哲学术语，别译成「人的本性」太啰嗦也行但「人性」最简洁）。and so on 须译出「等等」，它在评分里通常算到这个并列采分点里。"}]},{"n":42,"en":"The behavioral sciences have been slow to change partly because the explanatory items often seem to be directly observed and partly because other kinds of explanations have been hard to find.","refZh":"行为科学之所以变化缓慢，一方面是因为那些用来解释（行为）的因素似乎常常可以直接观察到，另一方面是因为其他种类的解释一直难以找到。","analysis":"","chunks":[{"en":"The behavioral sciences have been slow to change","lit":"行为科学一直变化缓慢","role":"（主干主谓（现在完成时））","note":"难点： have been slow to do = 迟迟未/一直慢于做某事 have been slow to change 不要直译「已经慢于改变」，地道译法是「迟迟未能改变 / 变化缓慢」。现在完成时强调「这个状态一直持续到现在」，与上文 we have been slow to develop the science 用法一致，呼应作者对行为科学的批评态度。"},{"en":"partly because the explanatory items often seem to be directly observed","lit":"部分原因是这些解释项目似乎常常可以被直接观察到","role":"（原因状语从句一（partly because 引导））","note":"难点： the explanatory items 指代回填：上文那些「心智、感受、性格」等解释项 explanatory items 是熟词僻义陷阱：item 在此不是「条目/物品」，而是「项目/项」。回看上句 states of mind, feelings, traits of character, human nature，the 是回指定冠词，items 指的就是这些「用来解释行为的（心智）项目」。译文里可译成「这些用来解释（行为）的因素/项目」，让读者知道指的是上文那些东西。seem to be directly observed 是被动 + 不定式，译「似乎可以直接观察到」即可，不要硬译「似乎是被直接观察的」。"},{"en":"and partly because other kinds of explanations have been hard to find.","lit":"部分原因是其他种类的解释一直难以找到","role":"（原因状语从句二（并列 and partly because 引导））","note":"难点： have been hard to find = 一直难以找到（现在完成时持续到现在） hard to find 是「难定语」结构（tough movement），逻辑主语是 other kinds of explanations 也是 find 的逻辑宾语，地道译法直接译成主动「难以找到」即可，不要译成「被找到」。两个 partly because 是「一方面……另一方面……」的并列，须翻译出对仗。"}]},{"n":43,"en":"The role of natural selection in evolution was formulated only a little more than a hundred years ago, and the selective role of the environment in shaping and maintaining the behavior of the individual is only beginning to be recognized and studied.","refZh":"自然选择在进化中的作用，仅在一百多年前才被系统地提出；而环境在塑造和维持个体行为方面所起的选择作用，则刚刚开始为人们所认识和研究。","analysis":"","chunks":[{"en":"The role of natural selection in evolution","lit":"自然选择在进化中的作用","role":"（前半句主语（含两层 of 介词短语））","note":"难点： of + in 双介词修饰名词 role：先 of 再 in 顺译 「the role of X in Y」是考研翻译高频结构，固定译「X 在 Y 中的作用」。natural selection（自然选择）和 evolution（进化）都是生物学固定术语，须直接用，不要意译成「自然挑选」「演化进程」。"},{"en":"was formulated only a little more than a hundred years ago,","lit":"（在）仅一百多年前才被提出","role":"（前半句谓语（被动语态 + 时间状语））","note":"难点： was formulated 被动转主动 / 译「才被提出 / 才得以阐明」 formulate 在此不是「制定（公式）」，而是「系统地表述/提出（理论）」——熟词僻义。was formulated 译被动「被提出」也对，但更地道是「才得以阐明 / 才被系统提出」。only a little more than a hundred years ago 不要漏「only」，它强调「不过才」的时间短，呼应作者「行为科学比生物学还晚」的暗示。"},{"en":"and the selective role of the environment in shaping and maintaining the behavior of the individual","lit":"而环境在塑造和维持个体行为方面的选择作用","role":"（并列句主语（结构与前半句平行））","note":"难点： selective role 与前半句 role of natural selection 在结构上故意平行：环境的「选择性」作用 selective role 不要译「有选择性的角色」，结合上文 It does not push or pull, it selects（环境不推不拉，而是「选择」）以及前半句的 natural selection（自然选择），此处 selective 是和「自然选择」对应的——环境对个体行为也起「选择」作用。地道译法是「环境……所起的选择作用 / 环境的选择性作用」。shaping and maintaining 是动名词并列作 in 的宾语，译「塑造和维持」并列动词。the individual 是抽象的「个体 / 个人」（生物学/心理学用法）。"},{"en":"is only beginning to be recognized and studied.","lit":"才刚刚开始被认识和研究","role":"（并列句谓语（现在进行被动 + 并列动词））","note":"难点： be beginning to be done 译「才刚刚开始被…… / 才刚刚开始为人……」 is only beginning to be recognized and studied 是「进行时 + 不定式被动」，地道译法是「才刚刚开始被认识和研究 / 才刚刚为人们所认识和研究」。only 同样强调「不过才」，与前半句的 only a little more than a hundred years 形成「一个一百年前就有了，另一个才刚开始」的对比，是本句的核心修辞——绝不能漏。"}]},{"n":44,"en":"They are the possessions of the autonomous(self-governing) man of traditional theory, and they are essential to practices in which a person is held responsible for his conduct and given credit for his achievements.","refZh":"自由和尊严是传统理论中的自主（自治）之人所拥有的特质，而且对于这样一种做法不可或缺——在这种做法中，一个人要为自己的行为承担责任，并因自己的成就而获得赞誉。","analysis":"","chunks":[{"en":"They are the possessions of the autonomous(self-governing) man of traditional theory,","lit":"它们（=自由和尊严）是传统理论中自主（自治）的人所拥有之物","role":"（前半句：主系表（They 跨句指代））","note":"难点： They 跨句指代「自由和尊严」+ possessions 抽象具体化 They 必须回上一句 Freedom and dignity illustrate the difficulty. 还原成「自由和尊严」，孤立译「它们」一定扣分。possessions of the autonomous man 不要硬译「自治的人的所有物」，结合语境（这里 possessions 是抽象概念「拥有的东西/特质」），地道译法是「自由和尊严是……自主之人所拥有的（特质 / 品质）」。autonomous 后面的括号(self-governing) 是同位语解释，无需译出括号本身，但需译出「自主的、即自治的」之义。of traditional theory 修饰 autonomous man，须前置成「传统理论中的自主之人」。"},{"en":"and they are essential to practices","lit":"并且它们（自由和尊严）对一些做法是必不可少的","role":"（并列分句主干（and 引导））","note":"难点： be essential to = 对……不可或缺；practices 取「（社会）做法 / 实践」义 essential to 是固定搭配「对……至关重要 / 不可或缺」。practices 在此不是「练习」，而是「实践 / 做法 / 惯例」（社会学常用义），熟词僻义。译时可处理成「自由和尊严对这样一些做法不可或缺」，留出后面 in which 从句的「这样一些做法」铺垫位。"},{"en":"in which a person is held responsible for his conduct and given credit for his achievements.","lit":"在这些做法中，一个人因自己的行为而被认为应负责任，并因自己的成就而被给予赞誉","role":"（in which 引导的定语从句，修饰 practices）","note":"难点： hold sb responsible for / give sb credit for 两个被动搭配 + 定从汉化 be held responsible for sth = 「因……而被追究责任 / 被认为应对……负责」；be given credit for sth = 「因……而被赞誉 / 被归功于」。两个都是被动，汉译可保留被动也可转「让某人承担责任 / 把功劳归于某人」。in which 定语从句较长（含两个并列被动），按汉语习惯不宜全部前置成「『……』的做法」，可拆出来译成「在这些做法中，一个人要……」，让句子读得开。"}]},{"n":45,"en":"Until these issues are resolved, a technology of behavior will continue to be rejected, and with it possibly the only way to solve our problems.","refZh":"在这些问题得到解决之前，行为技术将继续遭到抵制；而随之（被弃绝的），可能还有解决我们问题的唯一办法。","analysis":"","chunks":[{"en":"Until these issues are resolved,","lit":"（在）这些问题解决之前","role":"（时间状语从句（until + 被动））","note":"难点： until 引导否定持续 + these issues 跨句指代 until 在「主句为否定 / 将延续」的语境里，汉译要么译「直到……才……」、要么译「除非 / 在……之前，否则……」。本句主句是 will continue to be rejected（将继续被拒绝），表持续否定，固定译「（在）……解决之前 / 除非……解决」均可，前者更顺。these issues 须回上两句 It also raises questions concerning \"values\". Who will use a technology and to what ends? 还原成「这些（关于「价值」、谁来使用、用于什么目的的）问题」，孤立译「这些问题」考生看不懂、阅卷也会扣指代分。"},{"en":"a technology of behavior will continue to be rejected,","lit":"行为的技术将继续被拒绝","role":"（主句主谓（被动））","note":"难点： a technology of behavior 全文统一术语 + 被动转主动 a technology of behavior 全篇统一译「行为（的）技术」（与 41–44 题保持一致）。will continue to be rejected 译「将继续受到/遭到抵制 / 将继续不被接受」均可，比直译「将继续被拒绝」更地道——「抵制」对应学术界对一种新范式的态度。"},{"en":"and with it possibly the only way to solve our problems.","lit":"并且随之（被抛弃的）可能还有解决我们问题的唯一办法","role":"（并列结构（省略句：and with it [will be rejected] possibly the only way to solve our problems））","note":"难点： with it 的 it 回指 a technology of behavior + 省略主谓的并列 这是本卷最难一块，主体考生百分百卡这里。① with it 的 it 回指本句主语 a technology of behavior，意思是「随着这门技术（被拒绝）」；② and with it [will be rejected] possibly the only way…：这是省略句，省掉了和前句相同的谓语 will be rejected，译时需要补出来。地道译法：「随之（被拒绝的）可能还有解决我们问题的唯一办法 / 而解决我们问题的唯一办法可能也会随之被弃」。possibly 是态度词「可能、或许」，作者用它软化语气，不可漏译。the only way 的 only 是核心采分点——作者把行为技术看作「唯一」的出路，态度极强烈，必须译出「唯一」。"}]}]},{"id":"section3","kind":"writing","title":"Section III 写作","directions":"46. Directions: Study the following picture carefully and write an essay entitled “Cultures National and International”. In the essay you should 1. describe the picture and interpret its meaning, and 2. give your comment on the phenomenon. You should write about 200 words neatly on ANSWER SHEET 2. (20 points)","prompt":"46. Directions: Study the following picture carefully and write an essay entitled “Cultures National and International”. In the essay you should 1. describe the picture and interpret its meaning, and 2. give your comment on the phenomenon. You should write about 200 words neatly on ANSWER SHEET 2. (20 points)","points":20,"image":{"src":"assets/writing/2002-section3.jpg","alt":"这是一张照片，照片下方有一段文字说明“An American girl in traditional Chinese costume”","width":"683","height":"475","local":"assets/writing/2002-section3.jpg"},"model":{"essay":"The picture presents a young American girl who is smiling brightly. She is dressed in traditional Chinese costume, wearing an elaborately decorated headdress on her head and a pair of long earrings on her ears. Below the photo runs a line that reads: an American girl in traditional Chinese costume. Simple as it is, the picture conveys a profound message. The very fact that a Western girl is so charmed by Chinese attire suggests that a fine national culture is no longer confined within its national borders. Instead, it attracts and is shared by people all over the world. In other words, what is truly national is also international; the more distinctive a culture is, the more likely it appeals to the whole of mankind. As far as I am concerned, this phenomenon fully deserves our applause. In an age of globalization, cultures of different nations are flowing and blending as never before. A wise nation should take pride in and preserve its own cultural identity, while at the same time opening its arms to the merits of others. Only by keeping its unique character and joining the global exchange can a culture stay vigorous and truly enrich our shared world.","translation":"图中是一个年轻的美国女孩，笑容灿烂。她身穿中国传统服饰，头上戴着装饰繁复的头饰，耳朵上戴着一对长长的耳环。照片下方有一行文字写道：一个身着中国传统服饰的美国女孩。\n画面虽简单，却传递着深刻的信息。一个西方女孩如此为中国服饰所倾倒，这一事实本身就表明：优秀的民族文化不再被国界所局限，反而吸引着全世界的人、被全世界所共享。换言之，真正属于民族的，也属于世界；一种文化越有特色，就越可能打动全人类。\n在我看来，这一现象完全值得称赞。在全球化的时代，各民族的文化正以前所未有的方式流动、交融。一个明智的民族既应为自己的文化身份感到自豪、加以保存，又应向他者的长处敞开怀抱。唯有守住自己独特的本色、并融入世界的交流，一种文化才能保持活力，真正丰富我们共同的世界。","breakdown":[{"tag":"【第 1 段】","core":"白描落实描述任务","text":"【第 1 段】 白描落实描述任务 。本段用 presents / is dressed in 一般现在时客观白描，按人物—衣着—细节—图注顺序推进，末句 Below the photo runs a line that reads 把图下文字带出，三句话完成 describe the picture，不抒情、篇幅克制，为后文让路。"},{"tag":"【第 2 段】","core":"过渡引申点透寓意","text":"【第 2 段】 过渡引申点透寓意 。Simple as it is 一句由实入虚过渡，The very fact that... suggests that... 由画面事实推出普遍道理，末句 what is truly national is also international 直接回扣标题两个关键词，落实 interpret its meaning。"},{"tag":"【第 3 段】","core":"表态加背景加对策","text":"【第 3 段】 表态加背景加对策 。As far as I am concerned 明确亮出赞赏立场，In an age of globalization 提供背景依据，收尾 Only by... can a culture stay vigorous 给出守本色又敞开门的对策，完整完成 give your comment on the phenomenon。"}],"wordCount":201}}],"questionCount":40,"objectiveCount":40,"answerTable":{"ans-section1":"完形填空（四选一） Section I （1–20 题） 1 A between · 2 D until · 3 C medium · 4 B company · 5 B speeded · 6 A on · 7 D into · 8 D perspective · 9 C however · 10 B followed · 11 D although · 12 A apparent · 13 A institutional · 14 C capacity · 15 B in terms of · 16 D smaller · 17 A context · 18 C influenced · 19 B controversial · 20 C against \n（逐题解析见 完形填空（四选一）解析页\n）","ans-section2-part-a-1":"阅读理解（四选一） Section II Part A (1) （21–25 题） 21 C · 22 B · 23 D · 24 D · 25 A \n（逐题解析见 阅读理解（四选一）解析页\n）","ans-section2-part-a-2":"阅读理解（四选一） Section II Part A (2) （26–30 题） 26 C · 27 C · 28 D · 29 B · 30 C \n（逐题解析见 阅读理解（四选一）解析页\n）","ans-section2-part-a-3":"阅读理解（四选一） Section II Part A (3) （31–35 题） 31 B · 32 D · 33 D · 34 A · 35 A \n（逐题解析见 阅读理解（四选一）解析页\n）","ans-section2-part-a-4":"阅读理解（四选一） Section II Part A (4) （36–40 题） 36 B · 37 C · 38 B · 39 A · 40 D \n（逐题解析见 阅读理解（四选一）解析页\n）","ans-section2-part-b":"英译汉（划线句子翻译） Section II Part B \n主观题 · 参考范文与逐题解析见\n 英译汉（划线句子翻译）解析页","ans-section3":"写作 Section III \n主观题 · 参考范文与逐题解析见\n 写作解析页"},"coverage":{"objective":40,"explained":40,"missingSections":[]}};
